\subsection{Linked residual charge and complete-word storage}
\label{app:planar-complete-word-storage}
For an unmasked regular correction set $C=P-PH^TS^{-1}HP$, $A=I-KH$.
The actual tangent correction contains $f=dK\,r$. With $J=P^{-1}$,
$C^{-1}A=J$ gives the exact identity
\[
 \|Ae+f\|_{C^{-1}}^2=\|e\|_J^2-\|He\|_{S^{-1}}^2
                   +2e^TJf+\|f\|_{C^{-1}}^2.
\]
Thus the missing residual term cannot be removed by citing the homogeneous
factor word. Its covariance-induced part admits a useful \emph{linked}
bound with an exact constant:
\[
 f_P=A\,dP\,H^TS^{-1}r,\qquad
 \boxed{\|f_P\|_{C^{-1}}^2\le\tfrac12(r^TS^{-1}r)L_P},
\]
where
$L_P=\operatorname{tr}(P^{-1}dP P^{-1}dP)
-\operatorname{tr}(C^{-1}A dP A^TC^{-1}A dP A^T)$.
To prove this, put $Z=P^{-1/2}dP P^{-1/2}$,
$D=P^{-1/2}CP^{-1/2}$ and $E=I-D\succeq0$.
Then $D\succeq0$, and
\[
 L_P=2\operatorname{tr}(ZDZE)+\operatorname{tr}(ZEZE)
     \ge2\operatorname{tr}(ZDZE)\ge0.
\]
Writing $B=P^{1/2}H^TS^{-1/2}$ gives $BB^T=E$.
The $f_P$ energy is $v^TB^TZDZBv$, $v=S^{-1/2}r$;
it is at most $\|v\|^2\operatorname{tr}(ZDZE)$, proving the claim.
All operands are from the same literal operation; no unrelated maxima are
multiplied. In particular the covariance and mean ports are not independent.

For only this port, let $n=r^TS^{-1}r$, $V_P=\|Z\|_F^2$,
$L_x=\|He\|_{S^{-1}}^2$. Young's inequality yields, for $\lambda>0$,
\[
 W^+\le(1+n/\lambda)(V_x-L_x)+\lambda V_P
                   -\tfrac12(\lambda-n)L_P.
\]
The $nL_P/2$ square charge is retained. The remaining $dH,dR$, prediction,
reset, projection, AW and quotient-chart terms must still be included.
The optimal-correction identity is \emph{not} applied to the held-BA branch
with different gain and innovation operands.

For the complete coupled transverse-mean/covariance word write
$v_{i+1}=A_i v_i+B_i w$, with $w$ the \emph{same} persistent root/history
coordinate, including gauge forcing and curvature.
The literal nonlinear and arithmetic remainders are retained in this history
forcing when using the identity for finite deviations. Set
$M=A_{N-1}\cdots A_0$, $N_w=\sum_i A_{N-1}\cdots A_{i+1}B_i$.
For endpoint metrics $J_0,J_N\succ0$ the exact storage identity is
\[
 W_N-W_0=-v_0^TQv_0+2v_0^TXw+w^TZ_w w,
\]
where $Q=J_0-M^TJ_NM$, $X=M^TJ_NN_w$ and $Z_w=N_w^TJ_NN_w$.
Equivalently, $Q=\sum_i T_i^T(J_i-A_i^TJ_{i+1}A_i)T_i$, with actual ordered
prefixes $T_i$. This retains word cancellation and every cross term, including
moving precision-normalized quotient projectors; it is not an AW norm product.
If the inherited causal domain proves $Q\succeq\varepsilon J_0$, $0<\varepsilon\le1$,
then the derived complete-word inequality is
\[
 W_N\le(1-\varepsilon/2)W_0+
 w^T\left[Z_w+\frac2\varepsilon X^TJ_0^{-1}X\right]w.
\]
The same identities apply at every prefix. Their exact rational implementation
is \texttt{planar\_complete\_word\_storage.py}.

\textbf{Closure remains OPEN.} The frontend cone does not bound nominal
$\hat a_w$, innovation NIS, precision, or the linked $dH$/reset/AW word terms.
Consequently no positive uniform $\varepsilon$ has been established on the
inherited shipping domain. The result is an analytical loss/charge identity
and sufficient inequality, not a complete-word contraction certificate.
This is a D sufficient-bound limitation, not a shipping counterexample.
No radius or all-future magnetic floor is solved from an uncertified margin.
Structures preserved: full coupled derivative, actual covariance/innovation,
physical gauge and same-history forcing. Relaxations introduced: fixed regular
branches for differential identities; face crossings require finite inclusions.

\subsection{Inherited innovation comparison and coupled information coordinates}
\label{app:planar-innovation-storage}
These results enter the nominal-domain and complete-word-gap prerequisites,
\emph{before} any invariant-radius calculation. They neither assume a positive
word margin nor establish one. All correction identities below precede the
literal attitude injection, covariance reset and estimate projections.

\paragraph{Innovation comparison without independent residual maxima.}
For the actual innovation rows $H$, $P\succ0$, $R\succ0$, and
$S=HPH^T+R$, completion of the square gives, for every $z$,
\begin{gather*}
 J_c=P^{-1}+H^TR^{-1}H,\\
 \mathcal E(z)=\|z\|_{P^{-1}}^2+\|r-Hz\|_{R^{-1}}^2,\\
 \mathcal E(z)-r^TS^{-1}r=\|z-Kr\|_{J_c}^2.
\end{gather*}
Indeed the quadratic has Hessian $2(P^{-1}+H^TR^{-1}H)$ and minimizer
$(P^{-1}+H^TR^{-1}H)^{-1}H^TR^{-1}r=Kr$; substitution gives the stated minimum.
In held BA, $H$ here is the \emph{innovation} row including BA. Its virtual
minimizer need not be the applied masked gain. No gain is replaced.
If a physical comparison $z$ has $V=z^TP^{-1}z$ and
$r=Hz+\nu$, the immediate bound is
\[
 \mathrm{NIS}\le V+\nu^TR^{-1}\nu.
\]
There is no triangle-inequality cross charge between these two terms.

For the default zero-lever-arm, zero-temperature-slope accelerometer model,
write $R_{\rm true}=\exp([\vartheta]_\times)\widehat R$ and
$\delta a=a_{\rm true}-\hat a_w$. The physical-minus-nominal comparison
contains $\vartheta,\delta a$ and the SLOW BA difference. Its exact nonlinear
remainder, apart from delivered FAST/noise/arithmetic forcing, is
\[
 \nu_a=(e^{[\vartheta]_\times}-I-[\vartheta]_\times)
              \widehat R(a_{\rm true}-g e_z)
          +[\vartheta]_\times\widehat R\delta a.
\]
The integral Taylor formula and orthogonality of $e^{t[\vartheta]_\times}$ give
$\|e^{[\vartheta]_\times}-I-[\vartheta]_\times\|_2\le\|\vartheta\|^2/2$.
Hence, for a physical acceleration cap $A$,
\[
 \|\nu_a\|\le (g+A)\|\vartheta\|^2/2+\|\vartheta\|\|\delta a\|
                  \le z^TB_s z,
\]
where $s>0$, $(B_s)_{\theta\theta}=(g+A+s)I/2$,
$(B_s)_{aw,aw}=I/(2s)$, and other blocks are zero. This retains nominal AW
through $\delta a$; the physical cap has not been substituted for $\hat a_w$.
If the represented estimator gravity differs from physical $g$ by $\delta g$,
the additional exact term is $(I+[\vartheta]_\times)\widehat R\delta g e_z$;
it is included in the forcing cap, not absorbed into physical acceleration.
On a domain proving $B_s\preceq\kappa P^{-1}$, $R\succeq R_{\min}I$ and
additional residual forcing at most $d$, it follows analytically that
\[
 \boxed{\mathrm{NIS}\le V+(\kappa V+d)^2/R_{\min}.}
\]
The matrix domination uses the same actual covariance, including cross terms.
It is not a sampled covariance box. A uniform bound on $V$ and domination on
every inherited prefix are still required.

\paragraph{The literal first-Live boundary.}
One part of that inherited domain can be bounded without a replay. Consider
the central $\beta=0$ physical member with
$b_{a,s}=g(1-c)R_y(-\psi)e_z$, $c=39999/40001$, and physical $S(0)=0$ at
construction. This is the existing same-record family, not a new sensor
source. Work in the real-operation lift with represented configuration
scalars. Assume the retained private pitch/reference implication at handoff,
with $a_*=11/5000$; finite acquisition and float reference arithmetic are
not asserted here. The planar yaw is zero. Before first handoff, the wrapper
uses \texttt{updateFrontEnd}: it does not predict or correct the MEKF mean.
Thus the constructor's zero BG, BA and LIN means persist. The actual
\texttt{initialize\_from\_attitude} and \texttt{enterLive\_} then leave those
means intact, set the tilt/yaw covariance, seat AW on its current stationary
covariance, and keep BA held. No state is reseeded at a proof boundary.

Let $\widehat s$ denote the exact binary32 representation of the literal
configuration scalar $s$. The pitch axis is orthogonal to world down in
body coordinates, so its variance is $\widehat{.035}^{\,2}$ even though the
attitude block is anisotropic. The default horizontal factor is one and
the literal AW standard-deviation floor is $\widehat{.05}$. BA variance is
$\widehat{.004}^{\,2}$. All these blocks are decoupled at this boundary;
the untouched $v,p,S$ variances are $1,400,2500$. Put
$A_0=(1/50)(11/35)^2$ and $v_0=(1/50)(11/35)$, using $3<\pi<22/7$.
The \emph{inherited} physical primitive is
$S(t)=(1/50)(1-\cos(\pi t/10))/(\pi/10)$, so $\|S(t)\|<2/15$.
For every possible handoff phase the full 21-state comparison therefore obeys
\begin{align*}
 V_{\rm hand}\le{}&
 \frac{a_*^2}{\widehat{.035}^{\,2}}+v_0^2+
 \frac{(1/50)^2}{400}+\frac{(2/15)^2}{2500}\\
 &+\frac{A_0^2}{\widehat{.05}^{\,2}}
 +\frac{[g(1-c)]^2}{\widehat{.004}^{\,2}}
 <\frac{21}{1000}.
\end{align*}
Each cap applies to the same physical phase; this scalar outer majorant
does not declare independently chosen component extrema reachable. The
nonzero central BA and physical primitive charges are retained.
At these boundary operands, $\nu_a$ is bounded by
$(g+A_0)a_*^2/2+a_*A_0+(1+a_*)|\widehat{9.80665}-g|$.
The real reference cone implies
$\|B-75e_x\|\le75a_*(1+a_*^2/8)$, since
$\sqrt{1+a_*^2/4}\le1+a_*^2/8$. The magnetic remainder is at most
$75a_*^2/2+(1+a_*)75a_*(1+a_*^2/8)$.
Using $R_a=\widehat{.2}^{\,2}I$, $R_m=\widehat{.8}^{\,2}I$ in the
variational identity gives exact rational bounds
\[
 \mathrm{NIS}_{a,\rm hand}<21/1000,\qquad
 \mathrm{NIS}_{m,\rm hand}<13/200.
\]
These concern a correction evaluated at the first-Live boundary, before the
next prediction or other operation. They are \emph{not} bounds on a later
sample, on the whole H18 interval, or on A21. They establish neither a finite
handoff time nor float32 transfer. In particular they do not admit the physical
family or assert entry of its other compatible members into this small ball.

\paragraph{Reachable held-BA block.}
The literal hold setter zeros all BA--active cross covariances. Construction
already has that property. While held, prediction uses $\phi_{BA}=1$, adds no
BA process covariance and propagates zero cross blocks to zero. The default
CoG accelerometer update has $P=\operatorname{diag}(P_X,P_b)$, $X$ the other
18 coordinates, and literal operands
\[
 S=H_XP_XH_X^T+R_a+P_b,\quad
 B=\begin{bmatrix}P_XH_X^T\\0\end{bmatrix},\quad K=BS^{-1}.
\]
Substitution in the actual Joseph expression
$P-KB^T-BK^T+KSK^T$ shows that $P_b$ is unchanged and cross blocks stay zero.
Magnetic and $S$ corrections have no BA columns and preserve the same property;
reset acts on attitude only, AW sync adds to AW only, and estimate projections
do not change covariance. Default zero held BA mean is also preserved.
This proves the invariant block property by induction on literal operations
until release, excluding external covariance writes. On this reachable
manifold the active correction is optimal with $R_{\rm eff}=R_a+P_b$.
Thus the linked residual-loss lemma may be applied to this active block with
$dR_{\rm eff}=dR_a+dP_b$ retained. It may \emph{not} be applied to an arbitrary
held covariance with cross blocks, or extended past release by this argument.
All 21 states remain: held BA comparison error is still a residual/source port.

\paragraph{Coupled information coordinate.}
For the intermediate additive correction let $e$ now denote
nominal-minus-comparison state, where the comparison is unchanged during this
instantaneous operation. This sign convention is distinct from the physical
comparison $z$ above. Define the invertible tangent shear
\begin{gather*}
 \eta=de-dP P^{-1}e=P\,d(P^{-1}e),\\
 W_{\rm sh}=\|\eta\|_{P^{-1}}^2+
       \lambda\|P^{-1/2}dP P^{-1/2}\|_F^2.
\end{gather*}
For the unmasked optimal additive correction $e^+=e+Kr$ and $C=(P^{-1}+H^TR^{-1}H)^{-1}$,
$C^{-1}e^+=P^{-1}e+H^TR^{-1}(He+r)$. Differentiate this identity, including
$dH,dR,dr$, and multiply by $C$ to obtain, with $a=He+r$,
\[
 \boxed{\begin{aligned}
 \eta^+={}&A\eta+C\,dH^TR^{-1}a+K\,dH e\\
         &-K\,dR R^{-1}a+K(dr+H\,de).
 \end{aligned}}
\]
In the fixed-row, fixed-noise additive block, $dr=-H\,de$ gives
$\eta^+=A\eta$ for \emph{arbitrary} residual. The covariance-induced $dK\,r$
has cancelled algebraically against the derivative of precision; it has not
been discarded or bounded by unrelated maxima. The actual mean-dependent
rows and chart mismatch remain in the displayed formula. This is not an
additive model of finite physical attitude error: literal quaternion injection,
reset, projection and changing charts must be composed afterwards. Setting
$e^+=0$ by choosing a fresh comparison would destroy the identity.

If $e^TP^{-1}e\le E$ and $\lambda>0$, put
$C_E=\max(2,1+2E/\lambda)$. For
$W_0=\|de\|_{P^{-1}}^2+\lambda\|P^{-1/2}dP P^{-1/2}\|_F^2$,
\[
 C_E^{-1}W_0\le W_{\rm sh}\le C_E W_0.
\]
This follows twice from $\|u+v\|^2\le2\|u\|^2+2\|v\|^2$ and
$\|P^{-1/2}dP P^{-1}e\|^2\le E\|P^{-1/2}dP P^{-1/2}\|_F^2$.
Consequently the shear does not remove a direction, but uniform coercivity
still needs the inherited comparison domain. When $dP=0$ it leaves the physical
gauge tangent unchanged. Moving quotient projection, $C_Q\alpha$ and fibre
curvature must still be transported; they do not vanish in these coordinates.

For prediction $e^-=Fe+d$, $P^-=FPF^T+Q$, direct differentiation gives
\begin{align*}
 \eta^-={}&F\eta+F\,dP(Je-F^TJ^-e^-)
       +dF(e-PF^TJ^-e^-)\\
       &-FP\,dF^TJ^-e^-+dd-dQJ^-e^-.
\end{align*}
This retains the physical OU mismatch $d$ and its differential $dd$.
For the fixed-$F,Q$, zero-$d$ subblock only, its covariance port obeys
$\|f_P\|_{J^-}^2\le L_e L_P/2$, where
$L_e=e^TJe-(Fe)^TJ^-(Fe)$ and $L_P$ is the same prediction's Fisher loss.
To prove it put $U=(P^-)^{-1/2}FP^{1/2}$, $D=U^TU$, $E_0=I-D\succeq0$,
$Z=P^{-1/2}dP P^{-1/2}$ and $v=P^{-1/2}e$.
The port is $UZE_0v$, $L_e=v^TE_0v$, and
$L_P=2\operatorname{tr}(ZDZE_0)+\operatorname{tr}(ZE_0ZE_0)$.
Cauchy--Schwarz and the trace bound yield the claim. The zero-source subblock
does not impose the estimator OU model on physical truth; the other displayed
terms remain compulsory in the complete word.

The exact rational module \texttt{planar\_innovation\_storage.py} reproduces
these identities and boundary bounds. \textbf{OPEN:} carry that boundary
through actual H18, reference refinement, release and A21 with uniformly
coercive metrics, and bound the complete ordered word including all remaining
ports. No positive source-uniform $\varepsilon$ follows from the cancellation
or the first-boundary constants alone. No radius calculation is performed.
Structures preserved: actual innovation/gain/Joseph distinction, all states,
inherited physical primitive and BA, same-history covariance/residual, moving
gauge and literal reset/AW chronology. Relaxations introduced: explicitly
qualified real-operation identities, scalar outer boundary majorants and
Young's quadratic rotation-remainder bound. Failure classification for the
unclosed complete-word sufficient inequality remains D, not instability.

\subsection{Information-shear word action and compatible-tube transport}
\label{app:information-shear-word}
The governing order is symmetry/kernel identification, justified quotient or
compatible tube, linked dissipation, forcing, then the necessary activation
bounds. The general theorem assumes the existing MAGNETIC SERVICE premise;
it does not wait for the separate planar witness admission lemma.

\paragraph{Quantifiers and storage.}
For every finite regular real-operation shipping word, every differentiable
variation of its inherited history, actual positive covariance and innovation
matrices, and fixed $\lambda>0$, set
\[
 J=P^{-1},\quad \eta=de-dPJe,\qquad
 W=\eta^TJ\eta+\lambda\operatorname{tr}(JdPJdP).
\]
The comparison $e$ is inherited. This is a tangent identity; finite-error,
branch-crossing and arithmetic closure are not asserted. Write
$v=(\eta,\operatorname{vecsym}dP)$ and its metric as $\mathcal J$.
Split each actual operation exactly as $v^+=Lv+p$. The port $p$ includes
endogenous row/noise/source/reference dependence; it is not independent noise.
Auxiliary tangents are propagated causally or retained in the augmented root.

For a regular optimal correction, $L(\eta,dP)=(A\eta,A dP A^T)$,
$A=I-KH$, $C=AP$. With $a=He+r$, its ports are
\begin{align*}
 p_\eta={}&C\,dH^TR^{-1}a+K\,dH e-K\,dR R^{-1}a
                  +K(dr+Hde),\\
 p_P={}&-K\,dH C-C\,dH^TK^T+K\,dR K^T.
\end{align*}
These follow from Appendix~\ref{app:planar-innovation-storage} and the literal
optimal Joseph differential. Fixed rows/noise with $dr=-Hde$ cancel the
covariance-induced $dK\,r$ term. Reached held BA uses the active block with
$R_{\rm eff}=R_a+P_{BA}$, retaining $dR_{\rm eff}$ and held-bias ports;
the held covariance block has zero base loss. Arbitrary masked gains are not
replaced by optimal ones. Rejected corrections have identity transport;
solver repairs require their literal branch terms.

Prediction uses $L(\eta,dP)=(F\eta,FdPF^T)$ and the already-derived shear
port with physical OU mismatch, $dF,dQ$. Its covariance port is
$dFPF^T+FPdF^T+dQ$. For reset write the actual finite comparison as
$e^+=Ge+t$, $P^+=GPG^T$, with invertible shipping covariance reset $G$.
Direct differentiation, with no replacement of the finite injection by $G$,
gives
\[
 \eta^+=G\eta-GP\,dG^TG^{-T}Je+dt-dP^+(P^+)^{-1}t.
\]
The covariance port is $dGPG^T+GPdG^T$; the base congruence is an isometry.
Default AW has actual $P^+=P+U$, $U\succeq0$, $e^+=e$ and base identity:
\[
 \eta^+=\eta+dP(J-J^+)e-dU J^+e,\qquad dP^+=dP+dU.
\]
Here $dU$ retains the pending target and spectral face dependence. A face
crossing needs a directional or finite-increment inclusion. Bias projection
leaves $P$ unchanged: for its literal mean shift $s$,
$\eta^+=\eta+ds-dPJs$. No full-metric nonexpansiveness of Euclidean projection
is assumed. BG projection precedes injection; BA projection follows reset.
Reference/tuner/clock transitions retain their own tangents and branch choices.
The one-way Complementary result does not delete reference/gate feedback.
Watchdog jumps and unsupported covariance writes are outside this regular-word
identity until their literal maps are supplied.

\paragraph{Dissipation and its exact kernel.}
For prediction, correction or AW put
$U_0=(P^+)^{-1/2}BP^{1/2}$, respectively $B=F,A,I$.
Then $D=U_0^TU_0$ satisfies $0\preceq D\preceq I$; reset has $D=I$.
Set $E=I-D$, $y=P^{-1/2}\eta$, $Z=P^{-1/2}dPP^{-1/2}$.
The base storage decrement is
\[
 \ell(v)=y^TEy+\lambda\{2\operatorname{tr}(ZDZE)
                              +\operatorname{tr}(ZEZE)\}\ge0.
\]
Indeed the covariance output energy is $\operatorname{tr}(ZDZD)$;
expanding $I=D+E$ proves the formula. The two traces are respectively
$\|D^{1/2}ZE^{1/2}\|_F^2$ and $\|E^{1/2}ZE^{1/2}\|_F^2$.
Their simultaneous vanishing implies $ZE^{1/2}=0$, since $D+E=I$.
Hence zero loss is equivalent to $Ey=0$ and $ZE=0$. For optimal correction
this is exactly $H\eta=0$ and $H dP=0$. This characterizes base action,
not physical identifiability.

With $Q_i=\mathcal J_i-L_i^T\mathcal J_{i+1}L_i\succeq0$, expansion gives
\begin{align*}
 W_N-W_0&=-\mathcal A_W+\mathcal F_W,\\
 \mathcal A_W&=\sum_i v_i^TQ_iv_i,\\
 \mathcal F_W&=\sum_i\{2(L_iv_i)^T\mathcal J_{i+1}p_i
                                  +p_i^T\mathcal J_{i+1}p_i\}.
\end{align*}
No norm or independent extremum is taken. The square charge is compulsory.
The nonsheared alternative retains $\|f_P\|^2\le\mathrm{NIS}L_P/2$ only on
covered branches, with partial coefficient $(\lambda-\mathrm{NIS})/2$.
Variational NIS controls realized residual work, not arbitrary-direction
observability.

For actual causal prefix maps $v_i=T_i a$ in one augmented root/history
coordinate, define $E_i=T_{i+1}-L_iT_i$. Then
\begin{align*}
 G_A&=\sum_iT_i^TQ_iT_i,\\
 G_F&=\sum_i\{(L_iT_i)^T\mathcal J_{i+1}E_i+
                  E_i^T\mathcal J_{i+1}L_iT_i+
                  E_i^T\mathcal J_{i+1}E_i\},\\
 G_A-G_F&=T_0^T\mathcal J_0T_0-T_N^T\mathcal J_NT_N.
\end{align*}
The zero-action space is $\bigcap_i\ker(Q_iT_i)$, since every summand is
positive semidefinite. A trivial action kernel does not imply a positive full
gap until signed port work is controlled. The $T_i$ are complete coupled
prefix derivatives, not frozen $F/(I-KH)/G$ products.

\paragraph{Physical compatibility and moving quotient.}
A same-record physical variation leaves the deterministic estimator and $P$
unchanged. Its physical-error tangent need not vanish. In A21 the planar BA
tangent is constant while the estimator homogeneous transition multiplies it
by $\phi_{OU}$; the comparison therefore carries
$(1-\phi_{OU})r_{BA}$ as source. Thus it is not a homogeneous BA solution.
Where a regular A21 prediction has positive full process covariance, any
nonzero such tangent has positive base process loss; its forced work must
remain. This neither removes physical ambiguity nor proves instability.

On a proved fixed-rank compatible stratum let
$\Pi_G=R_G(R_G^TJR_G)^{-1}R_G^TJ$, $\Pi_\perp=I-\Pi_G$,
$\gamma=\Pi_G\eta$ and $\xi=\Pi_\perp\eta$. Then exactly
\[
 W_{\perp,N}-W_{\perp,0}=-\mathcal A_W+\mathcal F_W
                  +\|\gamma_0\|_{J_0}^2-\|\gamma_N\|_{J_N}^2.
\]
The terminal transverse map retains $\Pi_{\perp,N}M_{\eta\eta}R_{G,0}\alpha_0$
and all covariance/source ports. Rank changes need strata or a compatible-set
formulation. The planar line is not a universal gauge basis.
For $U=(R_G^TJR_G)^{-1}$ direct differentiation gives
\begin{align*}
 d\Pi_G={}&dR_GUR_G^TJ+R_GU\,dR_G^TJ+R_GUR_G^TdJ\\
           &-R_GU\,d(R_G^TJR_G)UR_G^TJ.
\end{align*}
In particular $d(\Pi_\perp e)=\Pi_\perp\eta+\Pi_\perp dPJe-d\Pi_Ge$.
The shear quotient therefore needs this conversion to physical distance,
including angle-to-precision bounds and the proved nonlinear fibre curvature.
For fixed source variation, the physical same-record tangent relation is an
affine forced relation; it is not asserted equal to the homogeneous kernel.

\paragraph{Precisely isolated uniform obligation --- OPEN.}
Let $\Gamma_i=T_i^T\operatorname{diag}(\Pi_{G,i}^TJ_i\Pi_{G,i},0)T_i$,
$J_{\perp,0}=T_0^T\mathcal J_0T_0-\Gamma_0$. On a justified root transverse
lift $B$ with $B^TJ_{\perp,0}B\succ0$, the required single linked inequality is
\[
 B^T(G_A-G_F-\Gamma_0+\Gamma_N)B
       \succeq c B^TJ_{\perp,0}B,\qquad c>0,
\]
uniformly for every activated admitted word. Auxiliary directions with zero
root storage must be retained as linked forcing or assigned justified storage.
MAGNETIC SERVICE supplies its specified transported physical-probe action;
the missing dependency is a quantitative comparison to this coupled sheared
action, together with process/$S$ action and absorption of signed work and
projector terms. No such uniform $c$ is certified here.

Where the two physical service directions have independent images in a
justified transverse stratum, complete them to root coordinates $(s,n)$.
Write $G=B^T(G_A-G_F-\Gamma_0+\Gamma_N)B$ and
$J=B^TJ_{\perp,0}B$, and partition $G-cJ$ as
$\left[\begin{smallmatrix}A_c&B_c\\B_c^T&N_c\end{smallmatrix}\right]$.
For $N_c\succ0$, the exact square completion is
\begin{align*}
 (s,n)^T(G-cJ)(s,n)
 ={}&(n+N_c^{-1}B_c^Ts)^TN_c(n+N_c^{-1}B_c^Ts)\\
 &+s^T(A_c-B_cN_c^{-1}B_c^T)s.
\end{align*}
Thus the missing uniform test is equivalently the positive complementary
block and positive semidefinite relative Schur complement on this branch.
A principal service floor does not bound that complement: actual cross terms
can cancel it. The blocks retain all signed shear work and cross precision.
If the service images lose rank, this coordinate stratum is not available.
No uniform constant is supplied by the algebraic reduction.

Only bounds needed for that comparison are activation obligations: required
precision/innovation comparisons; comparison energy and row geometry;
reference alignment and actual gates; injection chart and reset size;
AW/clock branch coverage; source/gauge and arithmetic charges; and finite
bootstrap with every-prefix containment. The qualified first-Live bound is
only a boundary lemma. No all-time compactness is assumed to prove itself.
The complete dependency table and persistent strategy are in
\texttt{docs/ou3-information-shear-strategy.md}; exact rational identities are
implemented by \texttt{information\_shear\_word.py}.

Structures preserved: all 21 mean states and covariance, actual optimal/held
Joseph distinction, physical forcing, injection/reset/projection/AW,
reference/gates/clocks and same-history moving compatibility.
Relaxations introduced: regular real-operation tangent scope with exact signed
ports; no surrogate execution or uniform finite-error theorem is asserted.
The unresolved sufficient uniform gap is classification D, not an admitted
counterexample. Invariant-radius and all-time planar service closure remain
open. Full planar admission would rule out universal eventual retention in the
specified absolute $V<.0225$ ball, not divergence or every larger practical bound.

\subsection{Same-record full covariance comparison}
Identical initial estimator state and delivered prefixes imply identical complete
internal executions by induction, including frontend, parameters, covariance,
gains, hard events and scheduler. No generated quantity is selected independently.
On the specified BA branch, let \(\bar p=1/1600\).
The literal initial/release variance and stationary OU variance are below
\(\bar p\). Held prediction preserves the diagonal and active prediction is
its convex combination with stationary variance. Regular Joseph corrections
cannot increase it; held zero BA rows, attitude resets and AW sync do not change
it. Thus \(P_{b_ay,b_ay}\le\bar p\) at every regular prefix of this branch.

For any SPD \(P\), Cauchy--Schwarz applied to
\(e_y^Te=(P^{1/2}e_y)^T(P^{-1/2}e)\) gives
\(e^TP^{-1}e\ge e_{b_ay}^2/P_{b_ay,b_ay}\).
Since \(\max\{|gs-\hat b_y|,|-gs-\hat b_y|\}\ge gs\),
\[
\max(V_+,V_-)\ge (gs)^2/\bar p=15.386492141376374\ldots.
\]
The pair cannot both have eventual retained \(V<.0225\) if both entire
continuations meet all premises. Establishing all-time actually applied
MAGNETIC SERVICE and execution totality for this pair remains open. The
102 carried one-second checks are evidence, not that certificate.
Structures preserved: the complete shipping record/chronology and full covariance
metric. Relaxations: only the explicitly stated quiet bias-charge ball outer;
no relaxation is used in the MOVING record identity or pair lower comparison.

\subsection{Moving-frame feedback and positive planar magnetic loss}
\label{app:measurement-frame-loss}
\paragraph{Quantifiers, role and scope.}
The following are analytical identities and qualified inequalities for every
regular real-operation word of the complete shipping CoG estimator. The
positive magnetic-loss assertion is restricted to nominal variations within
the proved planar stratum, with its even mean and block-diagonal even/odd
covariance. It is not a claim about all perturbations of a planar orbit.
Covariances and innovations are SPD. For held BA use the reached zero-cross
manifold, not an arbitrary masked covariance. Source, reference/noise and
branch variations not explicitly fixed below remain ports in the linked
word of Appendix~\ref{app:information-shear-word}. No estimator state is
reseeded, no physical premise is strengthened, and no replay constant is used.

\paragraph{Exact frame and differential.}
Let $R$ be the actual nominal world-to-body rotation and set
\[
 T=\operatorname{diag}(R,R,I,I,I,I,R),\quad
 \bar P=T^TPT,\quad \bar H=R^THT,\quad
 \bar R_m=R^TR_mR,\quad \bar r=R^Tr.
\]
Here the three rotating blocks are attitude, BG and BA; world $v,p,S,a_w$
are unchanged. The literal CoG rows become
\[
 \bar H_a=[-[\hat a_w-g e_z]_\times,0,0,0,0,I,I],\qquad
 \bar H_m=[-[B]_\times,0,0,0,0,0,0].
\]
The innovation, gain, increment and Joseph covariance transform by their
corresponding exact orthogonal congruences. The held BA row/column mask
commutes with $T$, so this assertion also holds for literal masked Joseph;
it does not turn an arbitrary masked update into an optimal Riccati update.
For $dR=R\omega$, $\omega=[d\vartheta]_\times$, and
$\Omega=\operatorname{diag}(\omega,\omega,0,0,0,0,\omega)$, differentiation gives
\begin{align*}
 d\bar P&=T^TdPT-\Omega\bar P+\bar P\Omega,\\
 d\bar H&=R^TdHT-\omega\bar H+\bar H\Omega,\\
 d\bar R_m&=R^TdR_mR-\omega\bar R_m+\bar R_m\omega,\\
 d\bar r&=R^Tdr-\omega\bar r.
\end{align*}
Thus the attitude-dependent row differential cancels exactly:
$d\bar H_a=[-[d\hat a_w]_\times,0,\ldots,0]$ and
$d\bar H_m=[-[dB]_\times,0,\ldots,0]$. Fixed isotropic measurement noise
has zero rotational noise differential. Anisotropic or changing noise does not.
Writing $\bar e=T^Te$, $\bar J=\bar P^{-1}$, the sheared coordinate satisfies
\[
 \bar\eta=T^T\eta-\bar P\Omega\bar J\bar e.
\]
Indeed $d\bar e=T^Tde-\Omega\bar e$; substitution of $d\bar P$ proves the
formula. Consequently the moving differential frame is not merely an
orthogonal transformation of $\eta$. Prediction/reset endpoint factors are
$T_{i+1}^TF_iT_i$ and $T_{i+1}^TG_iT_i$, with their full derivatives retained.
The AW covariance increment stays in the unrotated world AW block.

For fixed world $B$ and isotropic $R_m$, the magnetic additive substep has
\[
 \bar\eta^+=\bar A\bar\eta-
 \bar K(\omega\bar r+\bar H_m\Omega\bar e),\qquad
 d\bar P^+=\bar A\,d\bar P\,\bar A^T.                 \tag{MF1}
\]
This uses the literal same-model differential $dr=-H_mde$ in the pre-injection
chart; any additional chart/source mismatch is retained separately. It follows
by inserting the preceding pullbacks into the exact shear correction formula.
For every optimal correction,
\[
 K^TC^{-1}K=R_m^{-1}-S^{-1}=:D_m\succeq0.
\]
The magnetic port energy is therefore exactly $v^TD_mv$, with
$v=\omega r+H_m\Omega e$, rather than a product of independent gain and
residual bounds. Similarly the row-induced covariance port
$q=-K\,dH\,C-C\,dH^TK^T$ satisfies
\[
 \operatorname{tr}(C^{-1}qC^{-1}q)
 \le4\operatorname{tr}(C\,dH^TD_m dH).
\]
To prove it, write the whitened port as $-(X+X^T)$ and use
$\|X+X^T\|_F^2\le4\|X\|_F^2$. For the transformed accelerometer row this is
at most $8\lambda_{\max}(C_{\theta\theta})|d\hat a_w|^2/r_{\min}$, since
$D_m\preceq R_m^{-1}\preceq I/r_{\min}$ and
$\|[d\hat a_w]_\times\|_F^2=2|d\hat a_w|^2$.
The coefficient needs no independent nominal $a_w$ cap. Its absorption into
linked process/S loss, including the mean port, remains open.

\paragraph{Prior-observation covariance reader.}
On the regular planar branch the actual pitch/BG marginal has transition
\[
 F_y(h)=\begin{pmatrix}1&h\\0&1\end{pmatrix},\qquad
 Q_y(h)=\begin{pmatrix}q_g h+q_bh^3/3&q_bh^2/2\\
 q_bh^2/2&q_bh\end{pmatrix},                         \tag{MF2}
\]
where $q_g=\operatorname{RN}_{32}(.00135)^2$ and
$q_b=\operatorname{RN}_{32}(10^{-10})$. These are wrapper-profile constants:
\texttt{ProxyStartupFusionConfig::b0} is forwarded by
\texttt{initialize\_ext}; the standalone core default is different.
The positive BG cross sign is literal. About the $y$ axis, $R_{step,yy}=1$,
$B_{step,yy}=h$ and the Simpson integral of $s^2$ is exact. The pitch block
is positive definite and decoupled from the other four AG coordinates;
real spectral PSD repair does not alter its positive eigenvalues.
An additional $\varepsilon I_2$ per prediction, with
$\varepsilon=\operatorname{RN}_{32}(10^{-12})$, is a harmless covariance upper
relaxation, not a bound on floating-point eigensolver error.

A planar reset acts identically on pitch/BG covariance; AW changes neither
coordinate. BA/BG estimate projection does not change covariance. Other
optimal corrections decrease this marginal, also under the reached held-BA
active reduction. Each applied magnetic correction is a scalar pitch
observation with effective variance $\sigma_m^2/|B|^2$,
$\sigma_m=\operatorname{RN}_{32}(.8)$. Full cross covariance is retained in
this statement: the pitch marginal magnetic update depends only on that
marginal by parity. Riccati monotonicity therefore bounds it from above by a
magnetic-only two-state recursion with the same actual event times and noise.
An unbiased linear reader bounds that recursion regardless of the inherited
root covariance. This is covariance algebra; no physical history is required
to follow a Gaussian model or the estimator OU prior.

For observations at $t_1<t_2\le t$, put $\Delta=t_2-t_1$, $L=t-t_2$.
The reader
\[
 \hat\theta_t=(1+L/\Delta)y_2-(L/\Delta)y_1,\qquad
 \hat b_t=(y_2-y_1)/\Delta
\]
exactly reproduces $F_y(\Delta+L)$ on the two root coordinates, so its
root error is zero. If both observation variances are at most $r_m$, its
respective noise variances are at most
$[(1+L/\Delta)^2+(L/\Delta)^2]r_m$ and $2r_m/\Delta^2$.
For process noise between the events and after the second event, direct
integration of the reader kernels gives
\begin{align*}
 V_\theta^{proc}&=q_g(L^2/\Delta+L)+q_b(L^2\Delta+L^3)/3,\\
 V_b^{proc}&=q_g/\Delta+q_b(\Delta/3+L).                 \tag{MF3}
\end{align*}
For example, a BG impulse at age $s\in[0,\Delta]$ after the first observation
has pitch-error coefficient $-Ls/\Delta$ and bias-error coefficient
$-s/\Delta$. The corresponding gyro coefficients are $L/\Delta$ and
$1/\Delta$; on the tail the pitch/BG kernels are the usual integrator kernels.
Squaring and integrating proves (MF3), including their correlation.

The service premise supplies an applied event in each required one-second
IMU-rooted window. Set $h_{max}=3/500$ and choose the last IMU roots no later
than $t-3-h_{max}$ and $t-1-h_{max}$. Each lags its target by at most
$h_{max}$. Their windows end strictly before the correction at $t$. Hence
\[
 d_-=497/500\le\Delta\le d_+=1503/500,\qquad
 0\le L\le l=253/250.
\]
The required inherited service segment begins at least $3+2h_{max}=753/250$
seconds earlier; it contains no hard reset or unsupported covariance write.
The total reader horizon is less than four seconds. Every extra
$\varepsilon I_2$ has squared reader coefficient at most $3$, giving the
conservative charge $f=3\varepsilon(4/.004+2)$ for either variance.
With the retained cone $u=2^{-24}$, $a_*=11/5000$, put
\[
 b_-=75(1-u)(1-a_*^2/2),\quad b_+=75(1+u),\quad
 r_m=\sigma_m^2/b_-^2,\quad q=l/d_-.
\]
Substituting the endpoint bounds in the nonnegative expressions gives the
exact rational inequalities
\begin{align*}
 P_{\theta_y\theta_y}
 &\le[(1+q)^2+q^2]r_m+q_g(l^2/d_-+l)
       +q_b(l^2d_++l^3)/3+f<3/5000,\\
 P_{b_{g,y}b_{g,y}}
 &\le2r_m/d_-^2+q_g/d_-+q_b(d_+/3+l)+f<1/4000.       \tag{MF4}
\end{align*}
These bounds use no initial covariance ceiling and no nominal tilt bound.
The reference cone and service segment are qualified premises, not a proof
of planar admission or reference acquisition. Full arithmetic transfer is open.

\paragraph{Radial feedback and a strict linked correction loss.}
Now restrict the nominal variation and the inherited central-fibre comparison
to the planar stratum, keep the reference/noise fixed during this substep,
and omit bars. The comparison pitch and nominal pitch variation are both
along $e_y$, while $B,r$ lie in the $xz$ plane. Thus $H_m\Omega e=0$.
Also $KB=0$ for isotropic noise. With
\[
 \kappa=B^Tr/|B|^2,
\]
projection onto $B^\perp$ gives $K\omega r=\kappa KH_mde$ exactly.
Write the even-sector scalar row as $h$, its noise variance as $R_m$,
$s=hPh^T+R_m$, $t=hPh^T/R_m$, and $A=I-Kh$. Then (MF1) becomes
\[
 \eta^+=A\eta-\kappa Kh(\eta+dPJe),\qquad dP^+=A\,dP A^T.\tag{MF5}
\]
This retains the covariance-dependent work, not just the homogeneous mean
factor. The odd covariance block has its ordinary nonnegative Fisher loss.
The nominal tangent restriction does not discard that block or make claims
about nonplanar nominal directions.

Let $E=e^TJe$, $x=h\eta$, $z=h\,dPJe$,
$L_\eta=x^2/s$ and
$L_P=\operatorname{tr}(JdPJdP)-\operatorname{tr}(C^{-1}dP^+C^{-1}dP^+)$.
Whiten with $Z=P^{-1/2}dPP^{-1/2}$ and unit
$u_h=P^{1/2}h^T/\sqrt{hPh^T}$. Setting $v=P^{-1/2}e$ and
$\zeta=t/(1+t)$, the rank-one covariance loss is
\[
 L_P=2\zeta|Zu_h|^2-\zeta^2(u_h^TZu_h)^2
 \ge\zeta(2-\zeta)|Zu_h|^2,
 \qquad z^2/s\le E\frac{1+t}{2+t}L_P.                \tag{MF6}
\]
The $h=0$ case is immediate; all planar magnetic rows here are nonzero.
Expansion of (MF5), using $A^TC^{-1}K=h^T/s$ and
$K^TC^{-1}K=t/s$, proves, for covariance weight $\lambda>0$,
\[
 W^+-W=-aL_\eta-\lambda L_P
 -2\kappa(1-\kappa t)xz/s+\kappa^2t z^2/s,
 \qquad a=1+2\kappa-\kappa^2t.                       \tag{MF7}
\]
In particular the last square charge cannot be removed. Using (MF6), the
loss is bounded below by the quadratic form in
$(\sqrt{L_\eta},\sqrt{L_P})$ with matrix
\[
 \begin{pmatrix}a&-b\\-b&\lambda-\mu\end{pmatrix},\quad
 b^2=\kappa^2E\frac{1+t}{2+t}(1-\kappa t)^2,\quad
 \mu=\kappa^2Et\frac{1+t}{2+t}.
\]
The exact cancellation
$a\mu+b^2=\kappa^2E(1+t)^2/(2+t)$ illustrates why independent $K/r/P$
extrema lose the relevant structure.

For the retained six-degree nominal/central-physical pitch chart,
$|\alpha|\le\pi/30<11/105$. The reference angle is at most
$a_R=(1+u)a_*/[(1-u)(1-a_*^2/2)]$.
Componentwise magnetic sample rounding gives a vector error at most $75u$.
The radial ratio consequently obeys
\[
 \frac{1-(11/105+a_R)^2/2}{1+u}-\frac{75u}{b_-}-1
 \le\kappa\le\frac{75(1+u)}{b_-}-1,
 \qquad |\kappa|<3/500.                              \tag{MF8}
\]
This uses actual reference geometry, not the magnetic sensor-error bound as
an innovation bound. Equation (MF4) gives
$t\le b_+^2(3/5000)/\sigma_m^2<6$.
On the additional sufficient activation domain $E\le100$, choose $\lambda=1$.
Uniform rational bounds are
\[
 a\ge123473/125000,\quad \mu\le189/10000,\quad
 b^2\le4226103/1250000000.
\]
Both diagonal entries of the loss matrix minus $(9/10)I$ are positive;
its determinant is at least
\[
 (123473/125000-9/10)(1-189/10000-9/10)
 -4226103/1250000000=4673/1250000>0.
\]
Therefore
\[
 \boxed{W^+-W\le-\tfrac9{10}(L_\eta+L_P).}           \tag{MF9}
\]
This is a uniform positive \emph{operation loss fraction}, not a complete-word
contraction factor. The six-degree and $E\le100$ domain is not asserted
forward invariant; first-Live bounds cannot substitute for its retention.
Furthermore (MF4)--(MF6) imply
\[
 L_\eta\ge\frac{b_-^2}{7\sigma_m^2}\eta_{\theta_y}^2
 >1250\eta_{\theta_y}^2,
 \quad
 L_P\ge\frac{8b_-^2}{49\sigma_m^2}(dPJdP)_{\theta_y\theta_y}
 \ge1400(dPJdP)_{\theta_y\theta_y}.
\]
Use non-strict inequalities when the row vanishes. Thus (MF9) controls the
pitch row by $1125\eta_{\theta_y}^2+1260(dPJdP)_{\theta_y\theta_y}$.
These rational constants are derived here, not imported from finite evidence.

\paragraph{Word balance, zero action and exact remaining obligation.}
For the world $S$ row, $H_S\Omega=0$. On the proved default one-way tuner
path, MEKF-root variation has $dR_S=0$, so the additive $S$ substep loses
exactly $L_\eta+L_P$; source/noise and held-BA variations remain ports.
Split correction, injection and frame transport into their literal order.
With the same actual causal prefixes, (MF9) and the exact linked balance give
\[
 W_N-W_0\le-\widetilde{\mathcal A}_W+\mathcal F_{rem},\qquad
 \widetilde{\mathcal A}_W=
 \tfrac9{10}\sum_{mag}(L_\eta+L_P)
 +\sum_S(L_\eta+L_P)+\sum_{other}\ell_i.             \tag{MF10}
\]
The remaining work retains all signed cross and square terms from acc/AW-row
feedback, prediction and physical OU mismatch, $dF,dQ$, reset/frame changes,
projection, AW faces/targets, reference/noise changes and moving projectors.
It is not independent additive noise. At a covered magnetic substep the
coupled storage loss vanishes exactly when $h\eta=0$ and $h\,dP=0$ in the
even sector, together with the ordinary odd covariance loss kernel. Indeed
(MF6)--(MF9) force these conditions; conversely they give $z=0$ and zero
feedback in (MF5). Positive weights preserve the base word-action kernel.
This does not identify it with the forced physical compatibility family.
Same-record physical variation has $dR_{nom}=dP=0$, and carries physical
OU mismatch; its roll/BA direction is not the nominal planar-pitch direction.

For a justified transverse root lift $B_\perp$, use the action Gram
$G_{\widetilde A}$ from (MF10), the exact remaining signed work $G_{rem}$
and endpoint gauge-energy matrices $\Gamma_i$. The missing uniform statement
is precisely
\[
 B_\perp^T(G_{\widetilde A}-G_{rem}-\Gamma_0+\Gamma_N)B_\perp
 \succeq c B_\perp^TJ_{\perp,0}B_\perp,\qquad c>0.
\]
Positive pitch-row coercivity does not control all complementary directions.
Their process/S action and absorption of remaining work are open, as are
inherited reference/chart/energy activation, branchwise compatibility,
every-prefix nonlinear/float32 retention and source/gauge charges. No radius
is solved before those facts. General stability continues to assume existing
MAGNETIC SERVICE; this lemma neither proves nor disproves all-time admission
of the planar physical family.

Structures preserved: all 21 states, actual P/K/Joseph/masks, frame derivative,
reference/noise correlation, complete chronology and physical forcing.
Relaxations introduced: regular real-operation scope, qualified planar domain,
unbiased-reader covariance upper bound and rational Schur sufficient bound.
Neither arbitrary covariance nor independent physical histories replaces the
shipping execution. The exact algebra and rational certificates are reproduced
by \texttt{measurement\_frame.py}; tests alone are not the proof.

\subsection{Complete-word suffix score and linked covariance charge}
\label{app:linked-word-score}

\paragraph{Scope and quantifiers.}
For every finite regular real-operation word on one inherited shipping history,
let $P_i\succ0$, $J_i=P_i^{-1}$ and $D_i=dP_i$. Retain the exact differential
split
\[
 \begin{aligned}
 D_{i+1}&=B_iD_iB_i^T+U_i,\\
 de_{i+1}&=B_i de_i+B_iD_i d_i+v_i.
 \end{aligned}                                           \tag{WS1}
\]
The matrices $B_i$ are dissipative bases, not the complete Jacobians;
$U_i,v_i$ retain the actual complete causal variation, including auxiliary
feedback. No independently variable port or root covariance is substituted.
For an unmasked optimal additive correction, $B=A=I-KH$, $C=AP$ and
\[
\begin{split}
 d&=H^TS^{-1}r,\\
 U&=-K\,dH\,C-C\,dH^TK^T+K\,dR\,K^T,\\
 v&=dK_{H,R}r+K(dr+Hde),\\
 dK_{H,R}&=[P\,dH^T-K(dH\,PH^T+HP\,dH^T+dR)]S^{-1}.
\end{split}                                                    \tag{WS2}
\]
These follow from the literal gain and Joseph differentials. Reached held-BA
corrections use the proved active reduction with $R_{eff}=R_a+P_{BA}$,
$dR_{eff}=dR_a+dP_{BA}$ and retained held-bias ports, not an arbitrary masked
Riccati identity. The held coordinates are not declared contractive.
Prediction has $B=F$, $e^+=Fe+s$,
$U=dF\,PF^T+FP\,dF^T+dQ$, $v=dF\,e+ds$. Reset has $B=G$,
$P^+=GPG^T$, $e^+=Ge+s$, $U=dG\,PG^T+GP\,dG^T$, $v=dG\,e+ds$.
Default AW PSD addition has $B=I,d=0,U=d(\text{increment}),v=0$;
projection has $B=I,U=0,v=d(\text{shift})$. Physical/chart mismatch is
$s,ds$, not falsely equated to the covariance reset. Moving-frame connection,
reference, noise, branchwise solver changes and clock/face derivatives remain
in these ports. Nonsmooth branch crossings and arithmetic need separate
finite-increment qualifications.

\paragraph{Exact cancellation and word identity --- PROVED analytical.}
Let $M_{b,a}=B_{b-1}\cdots B_a$, $M_{a,a}=I$, and define
\[
 \begin{gathered}
 a_i=J_i e_i+d_i-B_i^TJ_{i+1}e_{i+1},\\
 q_{a,N}=\sum_{i=a}^{N-1}M_{i,a}^Ta_i.
 \end{gathered}
\]
Consecutive boundary terms telescope, giving
\[
 q_{a,N}=J_a e_a+\sum_{i=a}^{N-1}M_{i,a}^Td_i
                   -M_{N,a}^TJ_Ne_N.                         \tag{WS3}
\]
At an optimal additive correction, $A^TC^{-1}=J$, $JK=H^TS^{-1}$ and
$e^+=e+Kr$ imply $a_i=0$ for every residual. This identity does not require
$dH=dR=0$; their work remains in (WS2). A non-additive comparison shift $s$
adds $-A^TC^{-1}s$ to the score and $ds$ to its differential port.
For prediction, AW, reset and projection the respective scores are
\[
 \begin{gathered}
 (J-F^TJ^+F)e-F^TJ^+s,\quad (J-J^+)e,\\
 -G^TJ^+s,\quad -Js.
 \end{gathered}                                           \tag{WS4}
\]
Thus measurement residual cancellation does not remove physical OU mismatch
or nonlinear injection discrepancy.

Set $\eta_i=de_i-D_iJ_i e_i$. Direct substitution in (WS1) gives
\[
 \eta_{i+1}=B_i\eta_i+B_iD_i a_i+v_i-U_iJ_{i+1}e_{i+1}.
\]
Expand $D_i$ by variation of constants and interchange the finite sums. The
root covariance contributes $M_{N,0}D_0q_{0,N}$, while a covariance variation
born at boundary $i+1$ contributes $M_{N,i+1}U_iq_{i+1,N}$. Consequently
\[
 D_N=M_{N,0}D_0M_{N,0}^T+
       \sum_iM_{N,i+1}U_iM_{N,i+1}^T,                         \tag{WS5}
\]
\[
 \begin{aligned}
 \eta_N={}&M_{N,0}\eta_0+M_{N,0}D_0q_{0,N}\\
 &+\sum_iM_{N,i+1}
       [v_i-U_iJ_{i+1}e_{i+1}+U_iq_{i+1,N}].
 \end{aligned}                                           \tag{WS6}
\]
This proves the exact complete-word normal form. In particular, dropping
$U_iq_{i+1,N}$ loses later covariance-induced gain work generated by earlier
row/noise, reset or AW variation. Substituting (WS5)--(WS6) together into
$W_N=\eta_N^TJ_N\eta_N+\lambda\operatorname{tr}(J_ND_NJ_ND_N)$
preserves the previous exact action minus signed cross-plus-square work.
It is a regrouping of that identity, not an extra disturbance charge. The
magnetic work already absorbed in Appendix~\ref{app:measurement-frame-loss}
must not also be charged a second time.

\paragraph{Range-aware Fisher-loss charge --- PROVED analytical.}
For every $P,C\succ0$, matrix $M$ with
$G=P^{-1}-M^TC^{-1}M\succeq0$, symmetric $X$, and
$q\in\operatorname{range}G$, choose $Gz=q$ and set $\chi=q^Tz$.
The choice of solution does not change $\chi$. Then
\[
 \begin{gathered}
 \|MXq\|_{C^{-1}}^2\le\frac\chi2 L_P(X),\\
 \begin{aligned}
 L_P(X)={}&\operatorname{tr}(JXJX)\\
 &-\operatorname{tr}(C^{-1}MXM^TC^{-1}MXM^T).
 \end{aligned}
 \end{gathered}                                          \tag{WS7}
\]
To prove it put $D=P^{1/2}M^TC^{-1}MP^{1/2}$, $E=I-D$,
$Z=P^{-1/2}XP^{-1/2}$ and $\bar q=P^{1/2}q$. Then $0\preceq D\preceq I$,
$\bar q\in\operatorname{range}E$ and $\chi=\bar q^TE^\dagger\bar q$.
Expanding $I=D+E$ gives exactly
\[
 L_P=2\operatorname{tr}(ZDZE)+\operatorname{tr}(ZEZE)
 \ge2\|D^{1/2}ZE^{1/2}\|_F^2.
\]
Write $\bar q=E^{1/2}w$ with minimum $\|w\|^2=\chi$. The terminal
energy is $\|D^{1/2}Z\bar q\|^2$; Cauchy--Schwarz proves (WS7).
The range condition is essential. A score outside it has a component on a
zero-action direction, which must be retained as forcing, not discarded by a
pseudoinverse. It is not an admitted counterexample or permission to enlarge
the physical gauge.

There is a linked budget for the loss-generated score. Let
$Q_i=J_i-B_i^TJ_{i+1}B_i\succeq0$ and let $\mathcal L$ consist of
prediction/AW operations in (WS4). Set
\[
 \begin{gathered}
 q_{loss}=\sum_{i\in\mathcal L}M_{i,0}^TQ_i e_i,\\
 E_{loss}=\sum_{i\in\mathcal L}e_i^TQ_i e_i.
 \end{gathered}
\]
Stack $A_i=Q_i^{1/2}M_{i,0}$ and $w_i=Q_i^{1/2}e_i$. Since
$q_{loss}=A^Tw$ and $A^TA\preceq G=J_0-M_{N,0}^TJ_NM_{N,0}$,
the score lies in $\operatorname{range}G$. For $Gz=q_{loss}$,
$\chi=(Az)^Tw\le\sqrt\chi\sqrt{E_{loss}}$, so
\[
                         \chi(q_{loss})\le E_{loss}.        \tag{WS8}
\]
This uses the comparison and covariance of the same history. It is not a
bound from an independent nominal-state box or an observed NIS maximum.
The source/chart part $-\sum_i M_{i,0}^TB_i^TJ_{i+1}s_i$ retains its
sign and possible kernel component, including physical BA OU mismatch.

\paragraph{Inherited comparison budget --- PROVED analytical.}
The score budget (WS8) can itself be telescoped, rather than assumed as a
separate bound on every comparison state. Put $V_i=e_i^TJ_i e_i$ and, at an
optimal additive correction, $\delta_i=r_i+H_i e_i$. The inverse update and
actual gain give $J^+=J+H^TR^{-1}H$, $J^+K=H^TR^{-1}$ and
$K^TJ^+K=R^{-1}-S^{-1}$. Expanding $e^+=e+Kr$ therefore gives exactly
\[
 V_{i+1}-V_i=\delta_i^TR_i^{-1}\delta_i
                         -r_i^TS_i^{-1}r_i.                \tag{WS8a}
\]
This is an identity for the realized inherited comparison, not an
observability lower bound on arbitrary tangents. Reached held-BA uses the
active effective noise and retains the unchanged held comparison energy;
physical held-bias evolution is a prediction/source port.

For every other covered operation $e_{i+1}=B_i e_i+s_i$, direct expansion gives
\[
 \begin{split}
 V_{i+1}-V_i={}&-e_i^TQ_i e_i+\mathcal S_i,\\
 \mathcal S_i={}&2(B_i e_i)^TJ_{i+1}s_i+s_i^TJ_{i+1}s_i.
 \end{split}                                                \tag{WS8b}
\]
Take $\mathcal L$ to include all these noncorrection operations; reset and
unchanged-covariance projection have $Q_i=0$. Summing (WS8a)--(WS8b) and
using (WS8) proves, for every prefix as well as the complete word,
\[
 \begin{gathered}
 \mathcal S_W=\sum_{i\in\mathcal C}\delta_i^TR_i^{-1}\delta_i
                  +\sum_{i\notin\mathcal C}\mathcal S_i,\\
 \chi(q_{loss})\le E_{loss}
  =V_0-V_N+\mathcal S_W-\sum_{i\in\mathcal C}\mathrm{NIS}_i,\\
 \chi(q_{loss})\le V_0+\mathcal S_W
                              -\sum_{i\in\mathcal C}\mathrm{NIS}_i.
 \end{gathered}                                               \tag{WS8c}
\]
The same identity bounds $V_N$ after retaining the nonnegative
$E_{loss}$. No scalar bound on each intermediate nominal state is needed.
The signed work and innovation dissipation must remain linked: at a literal
$S=0$ correction with comparison $e_S=\widehat S-S_{phys}$,
$r=-\widehat S$ gives $\delta=-S_{phys}$, not zero. Neither the physical
primitive nor its supply is reset by the pseudo-measurement. Accelerometer
and magnetic $\delta$ likewise retain the actual physical/model/reference
mismatch. Upper-bounding their terms independently of NIS can lose the
cancellation and is not done here.

This reduces activation to root comparison energy plus a bound on the actual
signed comparison supply. The qualified first-Live central-fibre bound can
be used only when the word genuinely starts at that inherited boundary with
its hypotheses proved. It cannot be reused at later roots without a retention
argument. No uniform supply bound, source-score range property, generated-port
absorption or all-time compact domain follows from (WS8c) alone.

\paragraph{Conditional gap and minimal open dependencies.}
For the root part alone, suppose on a justified space that
$G\succeq cJ_0$, $0<c<1$, and the combined score has $\chi\le\chi_*$.
By (WS7) and $\|M\eta_0\|_{J_N}^2\le(1-c)\|\eta_0\|_{J_0}^2$,
the joint loss is bounded below by the quadratic form in
$(\|\eta_0\|_{J_0},\sqrt{L_P})$ with matrix
\[
 \begin{gathered}
 \begin{pmatrix}
 c&-\sqrt{(1-c)\chi_*/2}\\
 -\sqrt{(1-c)\chi_*/2}&\lambda-\chi_*/2
 \end{pmatrix},\\ \det=c\lambda-\chi_*/2.
 \end{gathered}                                          \tag{WS9}
\]
Thus $\chi_*<2c\lambda$ implies positive root-block loss. This is a
conditional implication, not a proved uniform complete-word gap. One still
needs a quantitative comparison of existing physical magnetic service and
process/$S$ action to a justified transverse lift; covariance-loss coercivity;
a uniform same-history comparison-loss/source score budget; and absorption of
the full generated ports in (WS5)--(WS6). Required reference/chart/energy and
branch margins must follow from inherited chronology. Only these quantities,
not unrelated absolute position/velocity boxes, are activation obligations.
The regular SPD scope is proved algebraically, not certified for all future
shipping prefixes. Reference accumulation, target libm and complete float32
transfer remain separate open premises.

Physical same-record variation has unchanged deterministic estimator/P, but
nonzero physical comparison and OU/bias forcing. It is not identified with
$\ker G$ or the joint action kernel. For a justified variable quotient retain
moving-projector derivatives, endpoint gauge energy and $C_Q\alpha$; handle
rank changes by valid strata or a compatible set. Frozen held-BA directions
require retention, not strict contraction. General dissipativity assumes the
existing MAGNETIC SERVICE premise; all-time admission of the planar witness
remains separate and open. No radius or uniform magnetic floor follows here.

Structures preserved: all 21 states, actual P/K/Joseph, reached held masks,
row/noise/innovation derivatives, covariance generated within the word,
reset/projection/AW and inherited source/reference/clock history.
Relaxations introduced: regular real-operation scope, then only the explicit
Cauchy--Schwarz sufficient bounds (WS7)--(WS9). No deployed behavior, profile,
constant or physical assumption is changed. The exact-rational regressions
in the information-shear word module validate these identities; the proof
is the derivation above, not the tests. Uniform full coercivity remains OPEN.

\subsection{AW shear, exact row cancellation and retained endpoint work}
\label{app:aw-shear-loss}

\paragraph{Scope and storage role.}
The following is an analytical identity for every regular real-operation CoG
word, in the complete nominal-world frame of
Appendix~\ref{app:measurement-frame-loss}. Actual covariance/gain/Joseph,
held masks, OU coefficients and inherited physical history remain unchanged.
It removes the accelerometer row-variation covariance port before taking
norms, while retaining the resulting endpoint and mean work. It does not
assert a complete-word gap or transfer the CoG wrapper profile to the
AtomS3R sketch with different settings or lever-arm terms.

Let $E_a,E_\theta$ select the AW and attitude blocks. Define
\[
 N(a)=-E_a[a]_\times E_\theta^T,\qquad L(a)=I+N(a).
\]
For every $a,b$, $N(a)N(b)=0$, so $L(a)^{-1}=I-N(a)$ and
$L(a+b)=L(a)L(b)$. There is no bound on $a$ needed for invertibility.
At the actual nominal $a=\widehat a_w$, set
$\widetilde P=LPL^T$, $\widetilde e=Le$, $\widetilde H=HL^{-1}$.
The literal rows become
\[
 \begin{split}
 \widetilde H_a&=([g]_\times,0,0,0,0,I,I),\\
 \widetilde H_m&=H_m,\qquad \widetilde H_S=H_S.
 \end{split}                                                   \tag{AS1}
\]
Thus all nominal AW dependence of the accelerometer row is removed.
Reference/noise variations are not removed. The transformation commutes with
the held-BA row/column mask; its gain, innovation and Joseph operands transform
exactly, including arbitrary held cross blocks. Optimal identities below still
require the reached held active reduction, with $dR_{eff}=dR_a+dP_{BA}$.
Mask congruence alone is not optimality.

\paragraph{Connection and exact cancellation --- PROVED analytical.}
Put $\Gamma=dL L^{-1}=N(d\widehat a_w)$. The complete differential is
\[
 \begin{split}
 d\widetilde P&=L\,dP\,L^T+\Gamma\widetilde P+
                                      \widetilde P\Gamma^T,\\
 d\widetilde e&=L\,de+\Gamma\widetilde e,\\
 \widetilde\eta&=L\eta-
           \widetilde P\Gamma^T\widetilde J\widetilde e.
 \end{split}                                                   \tag{AS2}
\]
It would be incorrect to transform the covariance tangent by frozen
congruence alone. Since $dH_a=H_a\Gamma$, its original row port obeys
\[
 \begin{split}
 U_H&=-K\,dH\,C-C\,dH^TK^T\\
 &=A(\Gamma P+P\Gamma^T)A^T-(\Gamma C+C\Gamma^T).
 \end{split}                                                   \tag{AS3}
\]
Indeed $C=AP=PA^T$, so the first half of the difference is
$(A-I)\Gamma C=-KH\Gamma C$, and the other half is its transpose.
This proves the connection-difference identity with its exact sign.
Consequently the additive correction, evaluated in its current $L$ frame,
has, for fixed noise,
\[
 d\widetilde C=\widetilde A\,d\widetilde P\,\widetilde A^T,
 \qquad
 \widetilde\eta^+=\widetilde A\widetilde\eta+
                                      \widetilde K m,            \tag{AS4}
\]
where $m=dr+\widetilde H\,d\widetilde e$. A noise variation adds its
literal $\widetilde K\,dR\,\widetilde K^T$ and mean noise port.
For the AW shear alone $m=(dr+Hde)+dH\,e$; for the preceding rotating
world frame, write its retained residual mismatch as $m_{extra}$ and obtain
\[
 m_a=m_{extra}-[\omega]_\times r-H_a\Omega e
                                  -[d\widehat a_w]_\times e_\theta.
                                                               \tag{AS5}
\]
Here all operands are from the same pre-correction world frame;
$\Omega=\operatorname{diag}([\omega]_\times,[\omega]_\times,0,0,0,0,
[\omega]_\times)$. Physical/source/chart variations are in $m_{extra}$.
The formula does not replace the full literal residual derivative by zero.

For $W=\widetilde\eta^T\widetilde J\widetilde\eta+
\lambda\operatorname{tr}(\widetilde Jd\widetilde P
                         \widetilde Jd\widetilde P)$, (AS4) gives exactly
\[
 W^+-W=-\|\widetilde H\widetilde\eta-m\|_{S^{-1}}^2
                -\lambda L_P+\|m\|_{R^{-1}}^2.                 \tag{AS6}
\]
To verify it, use $\widetilde A^T\widetilde C^{-1}\widetilde K
=\widetilde H^TS^{-1}$ and
$\widetilde K^T\widetilde C^{-1}\widetilde K=R^{-1}-S^{-1}$,
then complete the square. This retains all of the covariance Fisher loss,
with no independent AW-row charge or NIS cap. It does not make $m$ independent
forcing; its full signed quadratic work must remain in the word matrix.

\paragraph{No lost direction or erased physical gauge.}
At a fixed physical truth, choose the additive comparison orientation
$e_a=\widehat a_w-a_{phys}$. The transformed AW comparison is
\[
 \widetilde e_a=(I+[e_\theta]_\times)e_a-[a_{phys}]_\times e_\theta.
\]
The matrix $I+[e_\theta]_\times$ has determinant $1+\|e_\theta\|^2$
and inverse norm at most one: its squared norm on $v$ is
$\|v\|^2+\|[e_\theta]_\times v\|^2$. Thus this transformation of
$(e,P)$ is invertible on the existing attitude chart. It does not delete a
singular direction. Physical source variation retains the derivative of
$a_{phys}$ instead of resetting truth. Also
$\widetilde e^T\widetilde J\widetilde e=e^TJe$ exactly.
For the same-record physical fibre $dL=0$, because the nominal execution is
identical; its basis becomes $LR_G$, with unchanged precision Gram and gauge
amplitude. Neither homogeneous kernel equality nor physical identifiability
follows from the constant gravity row in (AS1).

\paragraph{Endpoint work and literal prediction are retained.}
A correction changes nominal AW by $\Delta a=K_{aw}r$. The required next-frame
map and its differential are exactly
\[
 \begin{split}
 B_L&=L(a^+)L(a)^{-1}=I+N(K_{aw}r),\\
 dB_L&=N(dK_{aw}r+K_{aw}dr).
 \end{split}                                                   \tag{AS7}
\]
Its covariance port is $dB_L\widetilde C B_L^T+
B_L\widetilde C\,dB_L^T$, and its mean/chart port follows the same literal
frame transport. A frozen factor product omitting (AS7) is not the complete
derivative. All parts enter the suffix-score identity (WS5)--(WS6), including
the downstream score of covariance created at this frame jump. No independent
bound on each AW norm or row increment is used.

For the literal OU prediction $a^+=\phi a$, retain the exact nominal-world
attitude covariance block $W_\theta$ and attitude/BG block $B_\theta$.
The transformed prediction $L(\phi a)F L(a)^{-1}$ has blocks
\[
 \begin{split}
 \widetilde F_{a\theta}&=\phi[a]_\times(I-W_\theta),\\
 \widetilde F_{ab_g}&=-\phi[a]_\times B_\theta,\\
 \widetilde F_{y\theta}&=F_{ya}[a]_\times,
                         \qquad y\in\{v,p,S\}.
 \end{split}                                                   \tag{AS8}
\]
These follow by block multiplication of the actual block-diagonal AG/LIN/BA
prediction. Do not replace $W_\theta$ by $I$: literal SO(3) coefficient and
mean-frame discrepancies remain. The BG and integrated LIN couplings are
not discarded. Process covariance is $L(\phi a)Q L(\phi a)^T$ with its full
differential, including same-history tuner variation. Reset uses both literal
endpoint rotation frames and the AW shear; projection retains its shift.

The default AW increment has support only on AW/AW, hence
$L\Delta_{aw}L^T=\Delta_{aw}$ and $\Gamma\Delta_{aw}=0$.
There is no new shear connection work at an AW sync whose mean is unchanged.
Its face is still evaluated on the original marginal recovered from
$L^{-1}\widetilde P L^{-T}$, not the transformed AW marginal. The actual
face/target derivative remains. This is not a new covariance floor law.

\paragraph{Physical substitution and linked curvature charge --- PROVED analytical.}
For the fixed-input central planar comparison, let $e_\theta=t e_y$,
$d\theta=\omega e_y$, $J_y=[e_y]_\times$, and
$R_{nom}^TR_{phys}=R_y(-t)$. This is the central physical pitch comparison,
not the roll/BA same-record gauge. The literal accelerometer equation gives
\[
 r+e_{BA}=-e_{aw}+(R_y(-t)-I)f_{phys}+\nu,\qquad
 f_{phys}=a_{phys}-g.                                      \tag{AS9}
\]
Here $\nu$ retains the existing delivered FAST and explicit model/arithmetic
source defects; no new unrestricted residual class is introduced. The nominal
BA estimate cancels before taking a norm. In (AS5), the two pitch rotations
commute, and $H_a\Omega e=\omega J_y e_{BA}$. Therefore
\[
 m_a=J_y\{t\,d\widehat a_w+\omega e_{aw}
                 -\omega t D(t)f_{phys}-\omega\nu\},       \tag{AS10}
\]
where $D(t)=(R_y(-t)-I)/t$, extended by $D(0)=-J_y$.
Since $\|R_y(-t)-I\|=2|\sin(t/2)|$, $\|D(t)\|\le1$ for all $t$.
The complete physical coefficient is retained; its phase is not varied
independently of the delivered history.

For the same nominal variation set $k=d\widehat a_w-\omega D(t)f_{phys}$
and let $B_v$ have column $k$ at pitch and block $\omega I$ at AW, all
other columns zero. Thus $m_0=J_yB_v e$ and $m_a=m_0-\omega J_y\nu$.
For every actual $P\succ0$ and $V=e^TP^{-1}e$, Cauchy--Schwarz in the same
covariance metric proves
\[
 \begin{split}
 \|m_0\|_{R^{-1}}^2
 &\le V\operatorname{tr}(R^{-1}J_yB_v P B_v^TJ_y^T),\\
 \operatorname{tr}(R^{-1}J_yB_v P B_v^TJ_y^T)
 &=p_{\theta\theta}k^TUk+2\omega k^TUc
                          +\omega^2\operatorname{tr}(U P_{aw,aw}),
 \end{split}                                                   \tag{AS11}
\]
with $U=J_y^TR^{-1}J_y$, $c=P_{aw,\theta_y}$ and
$p_{\theta\theta}=P_{\theta_y,\theta_y}$. To see the inequality directly,
write $e=P^{1/2}z$, $\|z\|^2=V$, and use the Frobenius bound on
$R^{-1/2}J_yB_vP^{1/2}z$. The signed covariance cross term is preserved.
No independent AW/BA estimate bound, covariance maximum or residual maximum
has been substituted. Source work is still exactly
\[
 \|m_a\|_{R^{-1}}^2=\|m_0\|_{R^{-1}}^2
 -2\omega m_0^TR^{-1}J_y\nu
 +\omega^2\nu^TJ_y^TR^{-1}J_y\nu.                         \tag{AS12}
\]
These terms enter the complete word together, not as independent extremes.
The necessary activation quantities for this port are now $V$, the linked
pitch/AW covariance block, actual physical force/rotation and the existing
source qualifications. The comparison budget (WS8c) supplies the exact
bookkeeping for $V$ but not its uniform numerical bound. Proving (AS11)--(AS12)
small enough after pairing with (AS7), process/$S$ and magnetic action remains
OPEN. No finite measurement value or new source constant is used.

\paragraph{Retained magnetic margin and exact open obligation.}
On the planar stratum the shear preserves parity, the attitude/BG marginal,
comparison energy, reference, residual and innovation. The rank-one magnetic
proof therefore applies in the new joint coordinates with the same qualified
$9/10$ loss, pitch/BG covariance bounds and activation conditions. Its proof
uses only these unchanged quantities and the identity
$de_\theta=\widetilde\eta_\theta+
(d\widetilde P\widetilde J\widetilde e)_\theta$.
The $S$ row remains fixed as well. These are not summed as losses from two
different storage functions: the complete word must use this one new storage.

The remaining gap requires the linked mean mismatch (AS5), actual correction
frame jumps (AS7), prediction/reset/source terms (AS8), noise/reference/AW
faces and moving-quotient terms to be included together. The inherited
comparison-energy budget (WS8c) is retained because point comparison energy
is unchanged. Uniform absorption and transverse coercivity are OPEN. No
radius, all-time planar admission or target-toolchain arithmetic closure is
asserted. Structures preserved: full 21-state P/K/Joseph/masks, OU and BG/LIN,
physical gauge, all derivative and inherited clock/source ports. Relaxations:
regular real-operation CoG scope and explicitly conditional activation only;
no estimator behavior or assumption change. Exact-rational regressions check
the noncommuting identities; this derivation, not the tests, proves them.

\subsection{Complete-word frame cancellation and the three-row endpoint test}
\label{app:aw-frame-word}

\paragraph{Lemma, quantifiers and role --- PROVED analytical.}
For every finite regular real-operation word, every differentiable linked
variation of its one inherited history, and every differentiable invertible
proof frame $L_i$, the following identities hold. Covariances are SPD and
$\lambda>0$. No source-uniform covariance ceiling, comparison-energy bound,
or contraction is assumed. This extends (AS7) through the whole literal word,
including prediction, BG/LIN coupling, reset, projection, reference/noise and
AW-face derivatives. It removes an accumulation of internal frame charges;
it does not remove their endpoint cost or any physical operation port.
Nonregular branch changes and arithmetic still require their own transfer.

Use (WS1), with $D_i=dP_i$, base $B_i$, gain score $d_i$ and actual linked
ports $U_i,v_i$. Set $C_i^L=L_i^{-1}dL_i$ and
$Z_i=C_i^LP_i+P_i(C_i^L)^T$. Direct differentiation, with no estimate, gives
\[
 \begin{split}
 \widetilde B_i&=L_{i+1}B_iL_i^{-1},\quad
 \widetilde d_i=L_i^{-T}d_i,\\
 \widetilde U_i&=L_{i+1}(U_i+Z_{i+1}-B_iZ_iB_i^T)L_{i+1}^T,\\
 \widetilde v_i&=L_{i+1}\{v_i+C_{i+1}^Le_{i+1}-B_iC_i^Le_i
                                      -B_iZ_i d_i\}.
 \end{split}                                                     \tag{FW1}
\]
Indeed substitute $\widetilde D_i=L_i(D_i+Z_i)L_i^T$ and
$d\widetilde e_i=L_i(de_i+C_i^Le_i)$ into both recurrences in (WS1).
The $-B_iZ_i d_i$ term is required by the covariance-dependent mean update;
it is not part of a frozen congruence. The local/suffix scores satisfy
$\widetilde a_i=L_i^{-T}a_i$ and
$\widetilde q_{i,N}=L_i^{-T}q_{i,N}$, since point comparison transforms by
$\widetilde e_i=L_i e_i$ and $\widetilde J_i=L_i^{-T}J_iL_i^{-1}$.

Iterating (FW1), or substituting it into (WS5)--(WS6), cancels every internal
$Z_i,C_i^L$. The exact terminal formulas are
\[
 \begin{split}
 \widetilde D_N&=L_N(D_N+Z_N)L_N^T,\\
 \widetilde\eta_N&=L_N\{\eta_N-P_N(C_N^L)^TJ_Ne_N\}.
 \end{split}                                                     \tag{FW2}
\]
This proof includes the term $U_iq_{i+1,N}$: deleting it prevents the
cancellation of generated covariance in the mean. It needs no invertibility
of the base $B_i$ and no optimality of an arbitrary masked operation. The
actual masked derivative, physical OU mismatch, $dF,dQ$, chart discrepancy,
projection and reference/face/target ports stay in $U_i,v_i$. In particular,
(AS8) is not replaced by a block-diagonal surrogate. The AW floor is still
computed on the recovered original marginal. The rotation-frame derivative
can either be included in a composed $L_i$ or retained in the input word;
these choices must not both be charged.

\paragraph{Exact boundary storage, with its sign retained.}
For a boundary put $J=P^{-1}$, $D=dP$, $C=L^{-1}dL$. Expanding (FW2) gives
$\widetilde W=W+\Phi$, where
\[
 \begin{split}
 \Phi={}&-2e^TJC\eta+e^TJCPC^TJe\\
 &+4\lambda\operatorname{tr}(DJC)
 +2\lambda\operatorname{tr}(C^2)
 +2\lambda\operatorname{tr}(JCPC^T).
 \end{split}                                                     \tag{FW3}
\]
For verification, write $y=P^{-1/2}\eta$, $z=P^{-1/2}e$,
$X=P^{-1/2}DP^{-1/2}$, $A=P^{-1/2}CP^{1/2}$. Then
\[
 \widetilde W=\|y-A^Tz\|^2+\lambda\|X+A+A^T\|_F^2.
\]
Expanding this sum proves (FW3), including the transpose in the covariance
cross term. Thus for the complete word, and for every prefix,
\[
 \boxed{\widetilde W_N-\widetilde W_0
              =-\mathcal A_W+\mathcal F_W+\Phi_N-\Phi_0.}        \tag{FW4}
\]
Here $\mathcal A_W,\mathcal F_W$ are the linked action and work in the input
frame. Alternatively one may use their fully transformed counterparts.
One may not keep the improved action in one frame while discarding its
corresponding work or the boundary difference. Internal connection ports do
not telescope as separate nonnegative charges: cancellation requires the
whole action-minus-work expression. Equation (FW4) removes an obligation to
bound the sum of individual frame jumps, not the remaining physical work.

\paragraph{AW specialization: exact three-dimensional signed quadratic.}
For the AW shear $C=N(a)$, $a=d\widehat a_w$, and $C^2=0$.
Let $C_j=N(e_j)$ for the three Euclidean basis vectors. Define
\[
 \begin{split}
 h_j&=-e^TJC_j\eta+2\lambda\operatorname{tr}(DJC_j),\\
 Q_{jk}&=e^TJC_jPC_k^TJe+2\lambda\operatorname{tr}(JC_jPC_k^T).
 \end{split}                                                     \tag{FW5}
\]
Then, exactly,
\[
 \begin{split}
 \Phi&=2h^Ta+a^TQa\\
     &=(a+Q^{-1}h)^TQ(a+Q^{-1}h)-h^TQ^{-1}h,\\
 \Phi&\ge-h^TQ^{-1}h\ge-W.
 \end{split}                                                     \tag{FW6}
\]
For $a\ne0$, $N(a)\ne0$, so the Fisher term gives
$a^TQa\ge2\lambda\|P^{-1/2}N(a)P^{1/2}\|_F^2>0$.
Hence $Q\succ0$. The last inequality follows by minimizing the displayed
nonnegative sum for $\widetilde W$ over the three formal connection variables.
This is only an algebraic bound; the actual $a$ is the inherited nominal
variation. The minimizer is not asserted reachable or introduced as a free
input. In particular (FW6) supplies a lower bound, not an affordable upper
bound for terminal work.

There is a smaller exact set of operands. Put $j_a=(Je)_{aw}$,
$J_{aa}=J_{aw,aw}$ and $B=(DJ)_{\theta,aw}$. Then
\[
 \begin{split}
 h_j&=j_a^T[e_j]_\times\eta_\theta
                            -2\lambda\operatorname{tr}(B[e_j]_\times),\\
 Q_{jk}&=\operatorname{tr}\{(j_a j_a^T+2\lambda J_{aa})
                   [e_j]_\times P_{\theta\theta}[e_k]_\times^T\}.
 \end{split}                                                     \tag{FW7}
\]
These formulas follow by inserting the AW/attitude selectors in (FW5).
They retain all covariance correlations through the actual precision.
In particular $J_{aa}$ is the inverse of the conditional covariance
\[
 P_{aa}-P_{ao}P_{oo}^{-1}P_{oa},\qquad o=\hbox{all non-AW coordinates},
\]
not $P_{aa}^{-1}$. The shipping marginal AW floor alone is not a proof of a
lower bound on this Schur complement. The qualified pitch variance ceiling
alone also does not bound the full $P_{\theta\theta}$ in (FW7). Even on the
planar stratum, $N(a)$ acts on both covariance parities; neither block is
silently deleted. No independent marginal maxima have been substituted.

\paragraph{Actual AW synchronization improves the required precision --- PROVED analytical.}
For every actual default PSD AW increment $\Delta\succeq0$, all non-AW and
cross blocks remain unchanged. With $o$ the non-AW coordinates put
$T=P_{ao}P_{oo}^{-1}$, $V_a=P_{aa}-TP_{oa}$ and
$v_a=e_a-Te_o$. Block inversion gives exactly
\[
 J_{aa}=V_a^{-1},\qquad (Je)_a=V_a^{-1}v_a,\qquad
 e^TJe=e_o^TP_{oo}^{-1}e_o+v_a^TV_a^{-1}v_a.
\]
The shipping synchronization changes $V_a$ to $V_a+\Delta$, while $T,v_a$
and $P_{\theta\theta}$ are unchanged. Consequently
\[
 \begin{split}
 J_{aa}^+&=(V_a+\Delta)^{-1}\preceq J_{aa},\\
 V_{cond}^+&=v_a^TJ_{aa}^+v_a\le v_a^TJ_{aa}v_a=V_{cond},\\
 \mathcal K^-(a)-\mathcal K^+(a)
 &=\operatorname{tr}\{(J_{aa}-J_{aa}^+)[a]_\times
                        P_{\theta\theta}[a]_\times^T\}\ge0,
 \end{split}                                                     \tag{FW7a}
\]
where $\mathcal K(a)=\operatorname{tr}(JN(a)PN(a)^T)$ is the exact
Fisher connection-square coefficient from (FW3). These inequalities follow
from inverse order for SPD matrices and the trace of a product of PSD
matrices. They hold for every face, including zero/rank-deficient increments;
no strict loss is asserted on inactive directions. Further, Cauchy--Schwarz
in the same conditional covariance gives
\[
 (Je)_a(Je)_a^T\preceq V_{cond}J_{aa},\qquad
 a^TQa\le(V_{cond}+2\lambda)\mathcal K(a).                       \tag{FW7b}
\]
Thus the actual AW synchronization cannot increase either factor in this
particular same-history endpoint-square majorant. This is a proved use of the
shipping floor; it does not replace its law by a floor on $V_a$, nor prove
an inherited numerical ceiling. The signed cross term $h$ and the complete
$Q$ need not be monotone. The nonincrease in (FW7a) is not a second decrement
to add to an already-accounted joint-storage loss.

At a differentiable active face, retain
\[
 \begin{split}
 dV_a={}&dP_{aa}-dP_{ao}P_{oo}^{-1}P_{oa}
                -P_{ao}P_{oo}^{-1}dP_{oa}\\
        &+P_{ao}P_{oo}^{-1}dP_{oo}P_{oo}^{-1}P_{oa},\\
 dJ_{aa}^+={}&-J_{aa}^+(dV_a+d\Delta)J_{aa}^+.
 \end{split}
\]
Here $\Delta=\Pi_+(\Sigma_{pending}-P_{aa})$ remains the literal recovered
original-marginal increment, including target/face and clock dependence.
The finite monotonicity statement does not assert differentiability at a
face crossing. Prediction, corrections and reset can change the conditional
blocks, so (FW7a) cannot be restarted as a universal precision bound.

\paragraph{A directional absorption threshold, not a new scalar campaign.}
Restrict every matrix below to the same justified stored root lift; auxiliary
directions with zero root energy remain forcing unless given justified storage.
On this lift write $h_i=H_i^L w$ and
$a_i=A_i^L w$, using the actual complete prefix derivatives, including
auxiliary/source coordinates where retained. Set
\[
 K_i^L=(A_i^L)^TQ_iA_i^L+(H_i^L)^TA_i^L+(A_i^L)^TH_i^L.
\]
Let $G$ be the input-frame exact word gap, and let $\Gamma_i$ now denote the
\emph{transformed} endpoint gauge-energy matrices. On stored transverse
coordinates with root metric $\mathcal J_\perp\succ0$, the required gap is
\[
 G+K_0^L-K_N^L-\Gamma_0+\Gamma_N\succeq c\mathcal J_\perp.
                                                               \tag{FW8}
\]
Completing (FW6) at the terminal endpoint defines
\[
 \begin{split}
 Z&=A_N^L+Q_N^{-1}H_N^L,\\
 R_c&=G+K_0^L+(H_N^L)^TQ_N^{-1}H_N^L
                  -\Gamma_0+\Gamma_N-c\mathcal J_\perp.
 \end{split}
\]
If $R_c\succ0$, (FW8) is equivalent to the \emph{three-row} test
\[
 \boxed{Q_N^{-1}-Z R_c^{-1}Z^T\succeq0.}                       \tag{FW9}
\]
Proof: (FW8) is $R_c-Z^TQ_N Z\succeq0$; apply the two Schur complements
of $\left(\begin{smallmatrix}R_c&Z^T\\Z&Q_N^{-1}\end{smallmatrix}\right)$.
The exact threshold is one for the squared singular norm of
$Q_N^{1/2} ZR_c^{-1/2}$, not an independent bound on each increment.
A common margin $\delta>0$ in
$Z R_c^{-1}Z^T\preceq(1-\delta)Q_N^{-1}$ would further give
$R_c-Z^TQ_N Z\succeq\delta R_c$.
No positive uniform $c$ or $\delta$ is certified here. If $R_c$ is not positive,
use the full signed (FW8); no inverse/pseudoinverse may erase a kernel.
Physical gauge amplitude and source directions are not optimized away by
this algebra, and frozen held BA still requires retention rather than strict
contraction.

\paragraph{Dependency removed and precise remaining obstruction.}
The need to price every $dB_L=N(dK_{aw}r+K_{aw}dr)$ separately is discharged:
(FW1)--(FW4) combine it with prediction and subsequent corrections before
norms, preserving every generated covariance score. The endpoint matrix
(FW7), its actual three-row tangent map and the remaining signed physical word
work are now the objects that must be absorbed. This calculation proves no
uniform domination of them by process/$S$/magnetic action. Appendix~\ref{app:aw-conditional-loss} supplies conditional precision on the
qualified LIN-path domain and positive base process loss on its conditional
AW block. The unavailable facts are the inherited activation and full
attitude-block comparisons actually needed by (FW7), the same-history comparison/source budget and
complete prefix derivatives, and the quantitative service-to-coupled-action
comparison giving a positive $R_c$ with the margin in (FW9). They are proof
obligations, not new physical premises. Reference/gates, finite-error chart,
arithmetic, moving compatibility and every-prefix activation remain required.

Structures preserved: full 21-state covariance and literal ports, both endpoint
frames, both parity blocks, held masks, actual AW face, same-history source and
all suffix scores. Relaxations: regular real-operation derivatives; the formal
completion in (FW6) supplies only its stated algebraic lower bound. No new
numerical exploration or independent reachable box is used. The complete-gap
attempt remains D (insufficient proved bound), not a shipping counterexample.
The qualified magnetic and physical-curvature results remain valid; they must
be evaluated in one consistent storage. General service-conditioned stability
and special planar all-time admission are still separate open obligations.

\subsection{Conditional AW storage, linked process loss and the unresolved endpoint margin}
\label{app:aw-conditional-loss}

\paragraph{Quantifiers and role.}
The block identities below hold at every regular real-operation boundary with
actual $P\succ0$, symmetric $D=dP$, $\lambda>0$, and linked comparison
$e,\eta=de-DP^{-1}e$. The strictly positive process bound additionally uses
exactly the existing isotropic regular-profile AW-ceiling and LIN-process
qualifications: $h\in[.004,.006]$, $\tau\in[.02,12]$,
$\sigma\in[.05,4]$, default additive AW synchronization and no reconfiguration.
They are implications on that inherited domain, not capture, float32, H18
release, or arbitrary-profile results. The obligation addressed is the
conditional AW block of (FW8), including the covariance tangent; the complete
endpoint Schur margin remains a separate signed matrix comparison.

\paragraph{Exact conditional decomposition.}
Reorder coordinates as $(o,a)$, where $a$ is the three AW coordinates and
$o$ contains the other eighteen. Define
\[
\begin{gathered}
 B=P_{oo},\quad T=P_{ao}B^{-1},\quad C=P_{aa}-TP_{oa},\\
 j=Je,\quad s=J\eta=d(Je),\quad \ell=s_o+T^Ts_a.
\end{gathered}
\]
Here $J_{aa}=C^{-1}$ is conditional precision. With $D=dP$,
\[
 dT=(D_{ao}-TD_{oo})B^{-1},\quad
 dC=D_{aa}-D_{ao}T^T-TD_{oa}+TD_{oo}T^T.
\]
The full joint storage splits exactly, with no deleted directions:
\[
\begin{split}
 W&=W_a+W_o,\\
 W_a&=s_a^TCs_a+\lambda\operatorname{tr}(C^{-1}dC C^{-1}dC),\\
 W_o&=\ell^TB\ell+\lambda\operatorname{tr}(B^{-1}dB B^{-1}dB)
       +2\lambda\operatorname{tr}(C^{-1}dT B dT^T).
\end{split}                                                     \tag{CA1}
\]
To prove this, factor
$P=\left(\begin{smallmatrix}I&0\\T&I\end{smallmatrix}\right)
\operatorname{diag}(B,C)
\left(\begin{smallmatrix}I&T^T\\0&I\end{smallmatrix}\right)$.
Congruence of $D$ by the inverse triangular factor gives diagonal blocks
$dB,dC$ and off-diagonal blocks $BdT^T,dTB$. The two off-diagonal products
in the Fisher trace give the factor two in (CA1). Expansion of $s^TPs$
gives its mean terms. All terms are nonnegative. This is a covariance
conditional decomposition, not a physical compatibility quotient.

\paragraph{What actual magnetic and integral corrections control.}
For every optimal additive correction with $H=[H_o,0]$,
\[
 J^+=J+H^TR^{-1}H,\qquad
 j^+=j+H^TR^{-1}(r+He).                                      \tag{CA2}
\]
Thus $J_{aa},J_{ao},j_a$ are unchanged, and consequently $C,T,j_a$
are unchanged. Differentiating this identity proves that $dC,dT,s_a$ and
$W_a$ are unchanged even for linked $dH_o,dR,dr$, provided $H_a=dH_a=0$.
The nominal-world magnetic and $S$ rows satisfy this restriction. The held-BA
case requires the reached active-block/effective-noise reduction; arbitrary
masked corrections are not covered. Injection/reset, changing world frame,
projection and branch crossings remain subsequent literal ports.

The endpoint coefficient in (FW7) has the form
\[
 Q_{jk}=\operatorname{tr}\{(j_aj_a^T+2\lambda J_{aa})
                 [e_j]_\times P_{\theta\theta}[e_k]_\times^T\}.
\]
The weight $j_aj_a^T+2\lambda J_{aa}$ is invariant in (CA2). Since the same
actual update has $P_{\theta\theta}-P^+_{\theta\theta}=K_\theta S K_\theta^T$,
for every $a\in\mathbb R^3$,
\[
 a^T(Q-Q^+)a=\operatorname{tr}\{(j_aj_a^T+2\lambda J_{aa})
 [a]_\times K_\theta S K_\theta^T[a]_\times^T\}\ge0.             \tag{CA3}
\]
This coefficient decrease is not a second storage decrement to add to the
already proved magnetic loss. In particular, the actual endpoint direction
changes by $b=d(K_{aw}r)$, so its signed work obeys instead
\[
 \Phi^+-\Phi=-a^T(Q-Q^+)a+2a^T(h^+-h)
       +2b^T(Q^+a+h^+)+b^TQ^+b.                              \tag{CA4}
\]
All quantities here belong to the same correction; $b$ is not a new input.
For fixed rows/noise on the additive substep, $\eta^+=(I-KH)\eta+Km$ and
$D^+J^+=(I-KH)DJ$ give the additional exact relation
\[
 h_j^+-h_j=-j_a^T[e_j]_\times K_\theta(H\eta-m)
       +2\lambda\operatorname{tr}(K_\theta HDJE_a[e_j]_\times).
                                                               \tag{CA5}
\]
Row/noise/reference variations add their literal derivative terms; (CA5)
does not discard them or apply unchanged when those operands vary.

For homogeneous fixed-row/noise additive transport, the subspace
$\ell=0,dB=0,dT=0$ is zero-action for all such non-AW measurements:
$\eta=E_aCs_a$ and $D=E_a dC E_a^T$ are unchanged by their base action.
It has three mean and six symmetric covariance coordinates. These are
algebraic storage directions, not nine physical gauges. They are retained,
and process action supplies their missing loss as follows.

\paragraph{Literal process comparison, including the integrated chain.}
Let $P^+=FPF^T+Q_p$, $J^+=(P^+)^{-1}$ and
$\mathcal L=J-F^TJ^+F\succeq0$. The actual AW row is
$E_a^TF=\phi E_a^T$, whereas $B_F=E_o^TFE_a$ includes the integrated
$v,p,S$ columns. Exact block expansion gives
\[
 \phi^2J^+_{aa}=J_{aa}-\mathcal L_{aa}-\mathcal C_{LIN},\qquad
 \mathcal C_{LIN}=\phi(J^+_{ao}B_F+B_F^TJ^+_{oa})+B_F^TJ^+_{oo}B_F.
                                                               \tag{CA6}
\]
For $\mathcal K(P,a)=\operatorname{tr}(J_{aa}[a]_\times
P_{\theta\theta}[a]_\times^T)$ this yields
\[
\begin{split}
 \mathcal K(P^+,\phi a)-\mathcal K(P,a)
 ={}&-\operatorname{tr}(\mathcal L_{aa}[a]_\times P^+_{\theta\theta}[a]_\times^T)\\
 &-\operatorname{tr}(\mathcal C_{LIN}[a]_\times P^+_{\theta\theta}[a]_\times^T)\\
 &+\operatorname{tr}(J_{aa}[a]_\times
             (P^+_{\theta\theta}-P_{\theta\theta})[a]_\times^T).
\end{split}                                                     \tag{CA7}
\]
The first term is loss. The other terms retain their signs and actual LIN/AG
correlations; BG coupling remains in $F$ and the full $J^+$. The relation
$da^+=\phi da$ applies to nominal-root variations on the proved one-way tuner
branch. A source/auxiliary variation adds $\widehat a\,d\phi$ and its exact
cross-plus-square work. It cannot be dropped from a source-uniform word.

\paragraph{A positive uniform process loss on the missed conditional block.}
There is a direct comparison stronger than merely asserting pointwise rank.
If the actual process matrix satisfies
\[
 Q_p\succeq FE_a q E_a^TF^T,\qquad q\succ0,
\]
then inverse order (the regular $F$ is invertible) gives
\[
 E_a^TF^TJ^+FE_a\preceq(C+q)^{-1},\qquad
 \mathcal L_{aa}\succeq C^{-1}-(C+q)^{-1}.                    \tag{CA8}
\]
The first identity uses the Schur complement of $P+E_aqE_a^T$;
it does not replace $C$ by the AW marginal.
For $q\succeq q_*I$, $C\preceq mI$, put $c_a=q_* /(m+q_*)$.
On the conditional block $\eta=E_aCs_a,D=E_adCE_a^T$,
\[
 \mathcal A_{p,a}\ge c_a s_a^TCs_a
   +(2c_a-c_a^2)\lambda\operatorname{tr}(C^{-1}dC C^{-1}dC)
   \ge c_a W_a.                                             \tag{CA9}
\]
Indeed $C^{1/2}E_a^TF^TJ^+FE_aC^{1/2}\preceq(1-c_a)I$ bounds
the mean quadratic and both sides of the symmetric Fisher tangent, hence
its squared factor $(1-c_a)^2$. This proves coercivity on the stated block;
for a general tangent, cross terms with its complement must still be kept.

Here $q_*$ can be made uniform using existing source bounds, without a new
sampled enclosure. Let $x=h/\tau$, $D_h=\operatorname{diag}(h,h^2,h^3,1)$,
and $f=D_h^{-1}F_{LIN}e_a$. The literal transition has $|f_i|\le1$:
for the exponential branch these are integrated exponential kernels;
for $x<.01$ the literal entries are
$1/2-x/6+x^2/24$ and $1/6-x/24+x^2/120$, both in $(0,1)$.
Let $B_0$ be the normalized zero-argument OU Gram matrix with entries
$2/(m!n!(m+n+1))$, $(m,n)\in\{1,2,3,0\}^2$.
Its exact inverse absolute row bound is $M=81060$.
The Volterra resolvent identity for the integrated exponential kernels gives
$B(x)\succeq B_0/(1+x)^2$: apply
$\|u+xVu\|_2\le(1+x)\|u\|_2$ with $\|V\|\le1$ to each kernel combination.
The existing literal small-$x$ certificate gives the relative covariance
error $\varepsilon<1$; outside that branch no truncation error is charged.
Consequently
\[
\begin{gathered}
 Q_{axis}^{ship}\succeq
 \sigma^2x\frac{1-\varepsilon}{(1+x)^2}D_hB_0D_h,\\
 (F_{LIN}e_a)^T(Q_{axis}^{ship})^{-1}F_{LIN}e_a
 \le\frac{4(13/10)^2M}{(1-\varepsilon)/1200000}.
\end{gathered}
\]
The rank-one Schur complement therefore proves the required process
comparison, with the integrated column intact, for
\[
 q_* =\frac{(1-\varepsilon)/1200000}{4(13/10)^2\,81060}>0.
                                                               \tag{CA10}
\]
The full process is block diagonal between LIN and AG/BA; their nonnegative
process contributions preserve this comparison, including held-BA zeros.
The existing isotropic AW ceiling gives
$C\preceq P_{aa}\preceq mI$, $m=16(1+\varepsilon)$ on its qualified
inherited profile. Exact rational evaluation gives
\[
 c_a=\frac{248188600375173268173354737}
 {2611278820575057006547769109785667114737}>10^{-14}.             \tag{CA11}
\]
This small but strictly positive base-action bound removes the unquantified
process-loss premise on the conditional AW block. It is not $c_{complete}$,
not an affordable bound on remaining work, and not a reason to run a scalar
constant-tightening campaign. No reachability of independently extreme tuner
values is asserted: (CA10) is a valid conservative lower bound for every
jointly generated tuple in the existing qualified range.

\paragraph{Conditional precision is finite on the qualified path domain.}
The existing 16-second LIN path certificate has scales $(2.4,18,132,4)$ and
matrix $A$, so $D_{LIN}E_{LIN}^TJE_{LIN}D_{LIN}\preceq A\otimes I$.
Thus $J_{aa}\preceq(A_{44}/16)I\prec15942618I$. The rational calculation
uses the committed path matrix, not a replay. Cross covariance is included;
this is a conditional precision bound, not $P_{aa}^{-1}$. Its regular A21
activation, noise floors and profile bindings must be inherited. It is not
an all-time H18/reference/chart or target-toolchain arithmetic theorem.

\paragraph{The exact obstruction remaining in the Schur test.}
(CA3), (CA7) and (CA9) give signed linked measurement/process terms and positive
conditional-block base loss. They do not establish $R_c\succ0$ in (FW9).
In particular, $G$ in that formula is the full action minus remaining linked
work, not an already positive matrix. On a justified stored lift use a
root-metric orthonormal basis, first for its intersection with the conditional
subspace and then its complement. Write the actual signed gap
$\mathcal G=G+K_0^L-K_N^L-\Gamma_0+\Gamma_N$ in that basis as
$\left(\begin{smallmatrix}D_a&X\\X^T&D_o\end{smallmatrix}\right)$.
For a proposed common $c>0$, the exact Schur conditions are
\[
 D_a-cI\succ0,\qquad
 D_o-cI-X^T(D_a-cI)^{-1}X\succeq0.                            \tag{CA12}
\]
If the first block is not positive, retain the full matrix inequality;
no inverse may erase a kernel. These are \emph{net signed} blocks, not
(CA9)'s base loss alone. The conditional block dimension on a constrained
lift is its actual intersection dimension, not an assumed new gauge rank. No bound on $X$
or the signed reductions of $D_a,D_o$ is supplied by a magnetic probe floor
alone. The still-unbounded terms are (CA4)--(CA7)'s coupled work, generated
covariance suffix scores, reference/noise/physical supply and moving gauge.
Frozen held-BA and un-stored auxiliary directions remain explicit retention
or forcing coordinates. Thus the positive endpoint Schur margin is OPEN.
Failure classification D: insufficient proved domination, no violating
shipping execution, no inferred instability and no invariant-radius claim.

Structures preserved: actual conditional precision and all cross covariance,
full integrated OU process, literal mag/$S$ gains, held effective-noise scope,
AW original-marginal floor, both frame endpoints, suffix scores and physical
history. Relaxations: regular real arithmetic; explicit existing profile
qualifications; a conservative rational lower bound only for the base process
block. No new physical assumption, gauge deletion, restart or runtime change.

\subsection{Actual signed conditional mixed blocks and a linked packet bound}
\label{app:conditional-mixed-word}

\paragraph{Lemma, quantifiers and activation.}
Consider any finite regular real-operation shipping word, beginning with a
prediction qualified by (CA8)--(CA11), followed by the actual dissipative
base maps and their complete linked ports. All boundary covariances are SPD;
reached held-BA reductions and invertible reset branches retain their stated
scope. Use one inherited history and the same fixed $\lambda>0$ throughout.
This lemma bounds the conditional-root mean/covariance mixed block and its
coupling to the remainder of the \emph{complete} tangent. It is subordinate
to the uniform finite-error word gap, not a finite-error theorem itself.
The process result proves invertibility of the base loss matrices used below;
it does not prove the signed score margin (CM4). No source, reference, reset,
AW-face or moving-gauge derivative is omitted. No enclosure or new physical
premise is used.

\paragraph{Actual three-dimensional compression.}
Let $E=E_{aw}$, $J_0=P_0^{-1}$, $J_N=P_N^{-1}$, and use the existing complete
suffix formula to define $M=M_{N,0}$ and $q=q_{0,N}$. Set
\[
 C=(E^TJ_0E)^{-1},\quad L=ME,\quad T=L^TJ_NL,\quad q_a=E^Tq,
 \qquad A=C^{-1}-T.                                           \tag{CM1}
\]
The full integrated process supplies
$A\succeq c_{aw}C^{-1}\succ0$: subsequent actual base maps satisfy
$B_i^TJ_{i+1}B_i\preceq J_i$, so their inclusion can only decrease $T$.
Thus this comparison includes actual process/$S$/magnetic closed-loop
transports and their whitening. It is not an open-loop row Gramian or a
replacement for the full tangent. On regular invertible base branches $T\succ0$.

For a symmetric conditional covariance variation $Y$ define
\[
 \mathcal F(Y)=C^{-1}YC^{-1}-TYT,\qquad
 K=T+TA^{-1}T=(T^{-1}-C)^{-1}.                               \tag{CM2}
\]
The previous process bound gives
$\langle Y,\mathcal F(Y)\rangle\ge
(2c_{aw}-c_{aw}^2)\operatorname{tr}(C^{-1}YC^{-1}Y)$.
All inverses in (CM2) therefore have a proved base-action justification on
this domain, rather than relying on pointwise numerical rank.

Choose the unscaled symmetric basis $E_j$ (both off-diagonal entries equal
one). Let $Y=\sum_j y_jE_j$, and define the actual six-dimensional Fisher
Gram and three-row score map by
\[
 (G_F)_{ij}=\operatorname{tr}(C^{-1}E_iC^{-1}E_j-TE_iTE_j),
 \qquad E_q y=Yq_a.
\]
For conditional mean coordinate $u$ and covariance coordinate $y$, the root
part of the signed word gap is exactly
\[
 \binom{u}{y}^T\mathcal D\binom{u}{y},\qquad
 \mathcal D=
 \begin{pmatrix}
 A&-TE_q\\
 -E_q^TT&\lambda G_F-E_q^TTE_q
 \end{pmatrix}.                                               \tag{CM3}
\]
This follows by subtracting the terminal energies of $L(u+Yq_a)$ and
$LYL^T$ from $u^TC^{-1}u+\lambda\operatorname{tr}(C^{-1}YC^{-1}Y)$.
In particular, the square of the covariance-generated mean score remains.
Completing the mean square leaves
\[
 S_\lambda=\lambda G_F-E_q^TKE_q.
\]
Since $A,G_F,K\succ0$, the two Schur complements of
$\left(\begin{smallmatrix}\lambda G_F&E_q^T\\E_q&K^{-1}\end{smallmatrix}\right)$
prove the exact equivalence
\[
 \boxed{\mathcal D\succ0\ \Longleftrightarrow\
 S_\lambda\succ0\ \Longleftrightarrow\
 \lambda K^{-1}-E_qG_F^{-1}E_q^T\succ0.}                       \tag{CM4}
\]
Non-strict inequalities give the corresponding semidefinite equivalence,
but a singular $S_\lambda$ does not justify the later inverse. No score is
removed by a pseudoinverse. Unlike (FW9), this test does not take the unknown
\emph{full net word gap} as an input: it uses explicit actual $C,T,q_a$ to
resolve just the conditional root score coupling. It does not resolve the
remaining generated ports.

\paragraph{Directional formula and a cancellation check.}
In coordinates making $C=I$ and $T=\operatorname{diag}(r_i)$, $0<r_i<1$,
the reader $B_q=E_qG_F^{-1}E_q^T$ is explicit:
\[
 (B_q)_{i\ell}=\frac{\delta_{i\ell}}2
       \sum_j\frac{q_{a,j}^2}{1-r_ir_j}
       +\frac{q_{a,i}q_{a,\ell}}{2(1-r_ir_\ell)}.              \tag{CM5}
\]
Indeed the inverse Fisher operator maps a symmetric entry $Z_{ij}$ to
$Z_{ij}/(1-r_ir_j)$, and the adjoint of $Y\mapsto Yq_a$ is
$v\mapsto(vq_a^T+q_av^T)/2$. This proves (CM5), including the essential
half factors for off-diagonal coordinates. Orthogonal diagonalization here
is an algebraic evaluation, not deletion of an inconvenient direction.

As a precisely delimited check, if $T=rI$ and the linked score is
$q_a=(1-r)e_a$, (CM4) is equivalent to
\[
 \lambda>\frac{r}{1+r}|e_a|^2.                               \tag{CM6}
\]
The factor $1-r$ cancels exactly. Replacing the score and process loss by
independent extrema would lose this cancellation. Equation (CM6) is an
algebraic isotropic relative-loss case; the shipping conditional covariance
is not asserted isotropic at every word. Use (CM4), not (CM6), generally.

\paragraph{All generated covariance and source ports in one linked packet.}
For the actual root tangent set
\[
 u=CE^TJ_0\eta_0,\quad
 Y=CE^TJ_0D_0J_0EC,\quad
 \eta_o=\eta_0-Eu,\quad D_o=D_0-EYE^T.
\]
The conditional decomposition (CA1) makes these complementary in the root
joint storage. Define from the complete actual terminal tangent
\[
 t=\eta_N-L(u+Yq_a),\qquad Z=D_N-LYL^T.                       \tag{CM7}
\]
Equivalently, using the proved suffix formula,
\[
\begin{split}
 t={}&M(\eta_o+D_oq)
 +\sum_iM_{N,i+1}\{v_i-U_iJ_{i+1}e_{i+1}+U_iq_{i+1,N}\},\\
 Z={}&MD_oM^T+\sum_iM_{N,i+1}U_iM_{N,i+1}^T.
\end{split}
\]
Every $U_i,v_i$ is the derivative of the literal operation on this same
history. In particular, $t,Z$ can depend on $u,Y$ as well as complementary,
source and auxiliary coordinates. They are not independent disturbances.
These formulas retain row/noise/reference variation, physical OU mismatch,
BG/LIN coupling, reset/projection and original-marginal AW-face derivatives.
They also retain source-score components outside the full base-action range.
No physical $S$, bias history or comparison state is restarted.

Put
\[
 b=L^TJ_Nt,\quad V=L^TJ_NZJ_NL,\quad
 h_j=q_a^TE_j(I+TA^{-1})b+\lambda\operatorname{tr}(E_jV).
\]
Let $W_o$ be the complementary root storage in (CA1). Direct subtraction
of the \emph{complete} terminal storage gives
\[
\begin{split}
 W_0-W_N={}&u^TAu-2u^T(TYq_a+b)
 +\lambda y^TG_Fy-q_a^TYTYq_a-2q_a^TYb\\
 &-2\lambda\operatorname{tr}(YV)+W_o
       -t^TJ_Nt-\lambda\operatorname{tr}(J_NZJ_NZ).
\end{split} \tag{CM8}
\]
Assuming the \emph{actual} strict score margin (CM4), two exact completions
now give
\[
\begin{split}
 W_0-W_N={}&\|u-A^{-1}(TYq_a+b)\|_A^2
          +\|y-S_\lambda^{-1}h\|_{S_\lambda}^2\\
 &+W_o-\mathcal P_{self}-\mathcal P_{mix},\\
 \mathcal P_{self}={}&t^TJ_Nt+\lambda\operatorname{tr}(J_NZJ_NZ),\\
 \mathcal P_{mix}={}&b^TA^{-1}b+h^TS_\lambda^{-1}h.
\end{split} \tag{CM9}
\]
The displayed identity remains exact after substituting the endogenous
functions $t(u,Y,\ldots),Z(u,Y,\ldots)$. It is not an optimization over
unreachable independent packets. Signs and cancellations are retained in
$t,Z,b,h$ before their linked quadratic charges are formed.

One may retain an explicit fraction of the positive root form rather than
merely drop the two completed squares. With $z=(u,y)$, the coupling vector
in (CM8) is
$\ell=(b,E_q^Tb+\lambda(\operatorname{tr}(E_jV))_j)$.
Block elimination proves
$\ell^T\mathcal D^{-1}\ell=\mathcal P_{mix}$.
For any $0<\beta<1$, the square
$\|\sqrt\beta z-\mathcal D^{-1}\ell/\sqrt\beta\|_{\mathcal D}^2$
therefore proves the rigorous actual mixed-work bound
\[
 W_0-W_N\ge(1-\beta)z^T\mathcal Dz+W_o
                  -\mathcal P_{self}-\beta^{-1}\mathcal P_{mix}.
                                                               \tag{CM10}
\]
In particular, $\beta=1/2$ gives one-half of the net conditional root loss
and exactly twice the linked mixed charge. This is not a product of
independent $K,r,P$ or per-operation suprema.

\paragraph{The conditional mixed reader is invariant under the actual AW frame.}
There is a further exact cancellation; it does not require a fixed frame.
Write $\mathsf L_i=I+N(\widehat a_i)$ and
$\Omega_i=\mathsf L_i^{-1}d\mathsf L_i=N(d\widehat a_i)$.
The literal shear has $\mathsf L_iE=\mathsf L_i^{-1}E=E$ and
$\Omega_iE=0$. Using the complete frame differential from (FW1),
\[
 \widetilde P_i=\mathsf L_iP_i\mathsf L_i^T,\qquad
 \widetilde\eta_i=\mathsf L_i(\eta_i-P_i\Omega_i^TJ_ie_i).
\]
It follows directly that
\[
 \widetilde C_i=C_i,\qquad d\widetilde C_i=dC_i,\qquad
 E^T\widetilde J_i\widetilde\eta_i=E^TJ_i\eta_i.
                                                               \tag{CM11}
\]
The last equality uses $E^T\Omega_i^T=(\Omega_iE)^T=0$;
it does not set $d\mathsf L_i=0$. Consequently the conditional coordinates
$u,Y$ and conditional joint storage are invariant. The complementary
storage changes by exactly $\Phi_i$, the previously retained frame work.

The exact base/score conjugacy also gives
$\widetilde M=\mathsf L_NM\mathsf L_0^{-1}$ and
$\widetilde q=\mathsf L_0^{-T}q$. Thus $C,T,q_a$, and hence every matrix in
(CM2)--(CM4), are unchanged. The actual transformed packets are instead
\[
\begin{split}
 \widetilde t&=\mathsf L_N(t-P_N\Omega_N^TJ_Ne_N),\\
 \widetilde Z&=\mathsf L_N(Z+\Omega_NP_N+P_N\Omega_N^T)\mathsf L_N^T.
\end{split}                                                    \tag{CM12}
\]
These terminal connection terms are retained before forming the packet
quadratics. Equations (CM9)--(CM10) can therefore be used entirely in the
AW frame with the same conditional root matrix $\mathcal D$, transformed
complementary root storage and transformed packets. No additional independent
AW endpoint penalty is needed in that accounting. This is not permission to
drop $\Phi_N-\Phi_0$ from the input-frame bound: it has moved into the actual
complementary storage and packets. Their endogenous dependence on $u,Y$
remains, so (CM11) alone does not prove a net block contraction.

\paragraph{Endpoint frame, quotient and remaining uniform obligations.}
When (CM9)--(CM10) are evaluated in the input frame, the AW-frame quotient
requires the exact adjustment
$\mathcal E=\Phi_0-\Phi_N-\Gamma_0+\Gamma_N$. When evaluated directly
with the transformed packets (CM12), add only $-\Gamma_0+\Gamma_N$;
the frame work is already included and must not be counted twice.
This retains actual endpoint frame derivatives, moving gauge and its forcing;
it does not claim that the conditional AW subspace is a physical gauge.
On a fixed justified lifted stratum, all packets and root coordinates are
linear maps of the same complete variation. Thus (CM10) is also a Loewner
lower bound on the corresponding actual signed mixed-block matrix, with
$\mathcal E$ kept as its signed root quadratic. It can be restricted to a
justified transverse lift, but no new lift or compatible-set rank is inferred.

The dependencies removed are the independent root mean/covariance score
estimate and separate bounds on each generated-port cross term. They are
replaced by the explicit three-row reader (CM4) and the aggregate quadratic
charges (CM9)--(CM10). The unresolved facts are a common strict (CM4) margin
for one $\lambda$ on the activated histories, and a same-history comparison
of $\mathcal P_{self}+2\mathcal P_{mix}-\mathcal E$ against complementary
process/$S$/magnetic loss and the retained conditional half-loss. The previous
$c_{aw}>10^{-14}$ proves $A,G_F\succ0$, not either of these net margins.
Inherited signed comparison supply bounds, reference/gates and arithmetic
activation remain open. In particular no positive $c_{complete}$, invariant
radius, finite-error retention or all-time planar admission is asserted.

Structures preserved: actual conditional precision, full covariance Fisher
metric, actual transported process/$S$/magnetic action, covariance created
inside the word and its suffix scores, original AW face, source/history and
both endpoint frames. Relaxations: regular real-operation branches and the
explicit sufficient inequality (CM10); no independent packet model, physical
assumption, runtime change or numerical exploration. D remains the status of
the unclosed uniform domination, not a shipping counterexample. A singular
score margin is retained as an obstruction to this inverse, not removed.

\subsection{Directional score limitation and automatic base-packet absorption}
\label{app:conditional-packet-absorption}

\paragraph{Scope and finite-error role.}
The following analytical result applies to every regular word covered by
(CM1), in either the input coordinates or the consistent AW coordinates
(CM11)--(CM12). It discharges absorption of the complementary packets of
its actual dissipative base transport. It does not replace the complete
tangent by that transport. A uniform directional score margin, endogenous
port absorption, quotient endpoint work and finite-error retention remain
separate obligations. No extra physical assumption or numerical enclosure
is used. In particular, positivity of the conditional process loss cannot
by itself establish those obligations.

\paragraph{Unequal directional losses do not share the isotropic cancellation.}
The limitation is an exact algebraic one. In the coordinates of (CM5), take
\[
 T=\operatorname{diag}(1-\varepsilon,1/2,1/2),\quad
 e_a=(0,a,0)^T,\quad q_a=(I-T)e_a=(0,a/2,0)^T,
 \qquad 0<\varepsilon<1.
\]
This preserves the loss-generated score relation; it does not choose a
score independently of its loss. Both $K$ and $B_q$ are diagonal. Equation
(CM5) gives the three eigenvalues of $K^{1/2}B_qK^{1/2}$ exactly:
\[
 a^2\frac{1-\varepsilon}{4\varepsilon(1+\varepsilon)},
 \qquad \frac{a^2}{3},\qquad\frac{a^2}{6}.                 \tag{CP1}
\]
Thus the strict score criterion requires $\lambda$ greater than their
maximum. In contrast, $q_a^T(I-T)^{-1}q_a=a^2/2$ is independent of
$\varepsilon$. The off-diagonal covariance variation linking coordinates
one and two transmits the strong-direction score into the weak mean loss.
A bound on comparison energy alone does not give a loss-independent
threshold. The existing positive $c_{aw}$ precludes taking
$\varepsilon\to0$ within its qualified fixed domain; it does not provide
the missing actual score bound. Equation (CP1) is a test of the logical
sufficiency of the retained matrix premises, not a reached shipping word,
an admitted counterexample, or a reason to tune $\lambda$ by a scalar search.
Its implication is to retain the actual directional reader and signed
supply; (CM6) cannot be extrapolated to anisotropic conditional losses.

\paragraph{Automatic absorption of complementary base packets.}
Equip the full mean/symmetric-covariance tangent space with the joint metric
$\mathcal H_i$ of $W_i$. Let
\[
 \mathcal T_0(\eta,D)=(M\eta,MDM^T)
\]
be the actual base transport, and choose root lifts $R_c,R_o$ with
$R_c(u,Y)=(Eu,EYE^T)$ and $R_c^T\mathcal H_0R_o=0$.
Keep the entire complementary space; it is not a physical-gauge quotient.
Set
\[
 D_b=\begin{pmatrix}A&0\\0&\lambda G_F\end{pmatrix},\quad
 B=R_c^T\mathcal T_0^T\mathcal H_N\mathcal T_0R_o,\quad
 H_o=R_o^T\mathcal H_0R_o,\quad
 Q_o=R_o^T\mathcal T_0^T\mathcal H_N\mathcal T_0R_o.
\]
Conditional process loss gives $D_b\succ0$. Full base nonexpansion gives
\[
 \mathcal H_0-\mathcal T_0^T\mathcal H_N\mathcal T_0\succeq0.
                                                               \tag{CP2}
\]
For completeness, whiten $M$ to $U=P_N^{-1/2}MP_0^{1/2}$.
The actual process/Joseph/reset/AW base inequalities give $U^TU\preceq I$;
hence $|U\eta|^2\le|\eta|^2$ and
$\|UZU^T\|_F^2\le\|Z\|_F^2$. This proves (CP2) on both mean and
covariance coordinates, including all cross-covariance entries. Held
coordinates remain, using only the reached optimal active reduction.
Congruence by $(R_c,R_o)$ and Schur complementation prove
\[
 \boxed{S_b:=H_o-Q_o-B^TD_b^{-1}B\succeq0.}                 \tag{CP3}
\]
Equivalently, for every complementary root $w$, the base packet energies
obey the actual joint inequality
\[
 \boxed{\mathcal P_{self,b}+\mathcal P_{mix,b}\le W_o,}
 \quad \mathcal P_{self,b}=w^TQ_ow,\quad
 \mathcal P_{mix,b}=w^TB^TD_b^{-1}Bw.                        \tag{CP4}
\]
This is source-uniform on the stated regular base domain with exact
coefficient one, requiring no full covariance ceiling or new service
constant. Equality and base kernels are allowed. It is not a positive
uniform transverse gap. The exact retained base loss is
\[
 W_0-W_{N,b}=\|z-D_b^{-1}Bw\|_{D_b}^2+w^TS_bw.             \tag{CP5}
\]
Thus one should not independently price propagation of the complementary
root a second time as generated forcing.

\paragraph{Why the fixed half-charge route is not a necessary test.}
A rational algebraic specialization suffices to check the loss of margin.
Take $P_0=P_N=I_2$, $E=(1,0)^T$, $q=0$, no covariance tangent or generated
ports, and
\[
 M=\begin{pmatrix}3/4&1/5\\1/5&3/4\end{pmatrix},\qquad
 \eta_0=(0,1)^T.
\]
The base eigenvalues are $19/20,11/20$, so the full base gap is strictly
positive. Nevertheless (CM10) with $\beta=1/2$ gives
\[
 W_0-W_N=\frac{159}{400},\quad
 \mathcal P_{self}=\frac{241}{400},\quad
 \mathcal P_{mix}=\frac{12}{53},\quad
 W_o-\mathcal P_{self}-2\mathcal P_{mix}
       =-\frac{1173}{21200}<0.                              \tag{CP6}
\]
The exact Schur remainder instead is
$159/400-12/53=3627/21200>0$. This formal test does not assert that these
matrices are shipping-reachable. It establishes a \textbf{D sufficient-bound
failure}: strict base contraction and the exact consistent-coordinate
identities alone do not imply the fixed half-charge domination. That
sufficient inequality remains valid, but must not be made a necessary
milestone or repeatedly tightened as if its sign were the true gap.

\paragraph{Exact remaining work and activation.}
Write the complete actual endpoint tangent, in the same coordinates, as
$\mathcal T_0v+\mathcal R(v,s)$, where $v=R_cz+R_ow$ and $s$ retains the
inherited auxiliary/source variation. The remainder includes $MD_0q$,
every generated $U_iq_{i+1,N}$, row/noise/reference derivatives, reset,
projection, original-marginal AW faces and endpoint connection terms.
No independence between these quantities is asserted. From (CP5),
\[
\begin{split}
 W_0-W_N={}&\|z-D_b^{-1}Bw\|_{D_b}^2+w^TS_bw\\
 &-2\langle\mathcal T_0v,\mathcal R(v,s)\rangle_{\mathcal H_N}
   -\|\mathcal R(v,s)\|_{\mathcal H_N}^2.
\end{split} \tag{CP7}
\]
In consistent AW coordinates add only $-\Gamma_0+\Gamma_N$ for the quotient.
The AW endpoint connection already belongs to $\mathcal R$ and the root
metric; it is not charged again. The unresolved threshold is domination
of the \emph{signed combined last two terms} and gauge work by (CP5),
with a strictly positive uniform remainder on a justified transverse lift.
Uniform score control still needs the inherited comparison and signed
source budget; first-Live energy cannot be restarted. Complementary
coercivity needs actual process/$S$/magnetic transport, not only magnetic
row rank. Auxiliary directions outside stored coordinates need their causal
lift or an explicit source/storage treatment. All-time branch activation,
nonlinear retention and arithmetic remain open. No radius is computed.

Structures preserved: full actual base covariance metric and transports,
all conditional/complementary covariance entries, complete signed generated
ports and endpoint frame/gauge work. Relaxations: (CP1),(CP6) are explicitly
formal tests of sufficient matrix implications, not models of the filter;
(CP2)--(CP7) use the proved regular real-operation identities without new
physical assumptions. No shipping counterexample is found. The uniform
score and complete signed-work gap are \textbf{OPEN}.

\subsection{Combined physical process score and causal generated-port loss}
\label{app:process-source-score}

\paragraph{Quantifiers and role.}
For every finite regular real-operation word on one inherited shipping
history, the identities below control the process score \emph{including}
its physical model defect. They then place $dF,dQ,ds$ inside a single
joint process balance, rather than independently estimating a gain,
residual and covariance. Boundary covariances are SPD. The score identity
allows PSD process covariance when the stated range condition holds;
the augmented differential identity below requires SPD process covariance.
Neither identity proves a uniform numerical budget or a complete positive
gap. They serve the remaining signed-work comparison with (CP5), without
reintroducing the failed half-charge test or an isotropic loss assumption.

\paragraph{The process score includes the physical defect.}
For actual operands write
\[
 C=FPF^T+Q\succ0,\quad e^+=Fe+s,\quad J=P^{-1},\quad J^+=C^{-1},
 \quad L=J-F^TJ^+F\succeq0,\quad a=Je-F^TJ^+e^+.
\]
Here $s$ is the \emph{actual} physical/model/chart comparison defect;
it is not zero merely because the estimator predicts with an OU model.
Assume $Q\succeq0$ and exhibit $t$ with $Qt=s$. Then
\[
 z=e-PF^Tt,\qquad Lz=a,\qquad
 \boxed{a^Tz=V-V^++s^Tt\ge0.}                              \tag{PS1}
\]
Proof: $LPF^T=F^TJ^+Q$, so $Lz=Le-F^TJ^+s=a$.
Expand $a^Tz$, using $FPF^T=C-Q$, to obtain
$e^TLe-2e^TF^TJ^+s+s^Tt-s^TJ^+s=V-V^++s^Tt$.
Since $L\succeq0$, $a^Tz=z^TLz\ge0$.
Thus $a\in\operatorname{range}(L)$ and
$a^TL^\dagger a=V-V^++s^TQ^\dagger s$, where both generalized-inverse
notations denote the already-verified range solutions, never kernel deletion.
The result is independent of the chosen solutions. No invertibility of $F$
is needed. Unsupported held-BA physical forcing, zero-noise chart shifts,
and projection defects do not satisfy this premise and remain explicit.

The positive $s^TQ^\dagger s$ is a physical comparison action, not an
assumption that physical truth is drawn from the estimator's process noise.
The existing source-qualified LIN action bounds use the actual committed
$\tau_k,\Sigma_{aw,k}$ and the identity
$u(t)=\dot a(t)+a(t)/\tau_k$, with the retained literal transition/noise
polynomial defects. They can be applied to this same action on their stated
domain. Their scalar amplitude relaxation is not asserted affordable for
the new complete-word margin.

\paragraph{A directional word bound without splitting loss and source scores.}
Let $\mathcal C$ be the covered process/PSD-addition operations, and let
$M_{i,0}$ be the actual base prefixes. Define
\[
 q_c=\sum_{i\in\mathcal C}M_{i,0}^Ta_i,\quad
 G=J_0-M_{N,0}^TJ_NM_{N,0},\quad
 B_W=\sum_{i\in\mathcal C}a_i^TL_i^\dagger a_i.
\]
Actual optimal additive corrections have zero local suffix score, as proved
in the preceding appendix. Collect all uncovered local scores, including
chart/held/projection terms, in $q_u$; the total score is $q=q_c+q_u$.
Then
\[
 \boxed{q_cq_c^T\preceq B_W G,\qquad
 q_c\in\operatorname{range}(G),\qquad
 q_c^TG^\dagger q_c\le B_W.}                                \tag{PS2}
\]
For a proof, set $X_i=L_i^{1/2}M_{i,0}$ and
$h_i=L_i^{1/2}z_i$, where $L_iz_i=a_i$ from (PS1).
After stacking, $q_c=X^Th$, $|h|^2=B_W$, and
$X^TX\preceq G$ by exact telescoping of all base losses. Cauchy--Schwarz
in \emph{each retained direction} proves (PS2). This controls the combined
physical score, rather than only the old loss-generated part.

Let $\mathcal M$ be the optimal additive substeps and $\mathcal U$ the
uncovered operations. The budget also telescopes exactly:
\[
\begin{split}
 B_W={}&V_0-V_N+\sum_{i\in\mathcal C}s_i^TQ_i^\dagger s_i\\
 &+\sum_{i\in\mathcal M}
   (\delta_i^TR_i^{-1}\delta_i-\mathrm{NIS}_i)
   +\sum_{i\in\mathcal U}(V_{i+1}-V_i),\qquad
 \delta_i=r_i+H_ie_i.
\end{split}                                                   \tag{PS3}
\]
This follows by summing (PS1) and the existing correction comparison identity.
The last sum is signed. It is not dropped, estimated by unrelated coordinate
maxima, or silently set to zero. In particular, the $S=0$ physical defect is
$-S_{physical}$. Initialization and every physical/source primitive are
inherited. The first-Live bound cannot be reapplied at a later word root.

For the conditional AW selector $E$, (PS2) yields
$(E^Tq_c)(E^Tq_c)^T\preceq B_W A$. The \emph{actual} directional reader in
(CM4) must still use $q_a=E^Tq_c+E^Tq_u$. Because $E_q$ is linear in $q$,
its reader includes both signed bilinear terms
\[
 E_{q_c}G_F^{-1}E_{q_u}^T+E_{q_u}G_F^{-1}E_{q_c}^T
\]
(with the conditional projections understood), as well as both squares.
No pseudoinverse or independent score cap removes these terms. In particular,
(PS2) is not itself the anisotropic strict margin (CM4).

\paragraph{One factorization of all literal generated process ports.}
Now assume $Q\succ0$ on the covered substep, and write
$D=dP$, $F_1=dF$, $Q_1=dQ$, $s_1=ds$. The actual derivative is
\[
 D^+=FDF^T+F_1PF^T+FPF_1^T+Q_1,\qquad
 de^+=Fde+F_1e+s_1.                                         \tag{PS4}
\]
These derivatives are generated by the same full history, not independent
perturbations. Introduce only an \emph{algebraic} augmented covariance and
linear channel:
\[
 \Sigma=\begin{pmatrix}P&0\\0&Q\end{pmatrix},\quad
 X=\begin{pmatrix}D&PF_1^T\\F_1P&Q_1\end{pmatrix},\quad
 T=[F\ I],\quad z=\binom e s,
\]
\[
 \nu=s_1-Q_1Q^{-1}s,\qquad
 \zeta=\binom{\eta-PF_1^TQ^{-1}s}{\nu},\qquad
 \Lambda=\Sigma^{-1}-T^TC^{-1}T\succeq0.
\]
Direct multiplication gives the complete identities
\[
 D^+=TXT^T,\qquad \eta^+=T\zeta+f,\qquad f=TX\Lambda z.     \tag{PS5}
\]
For verification, the augmented mean derivative is
$(de,s_1+F_1e)$ and its information shear is precisely $\zeta$;
applying $T$ then yields (PS4)--(PS5). This factorization does not introduce
an independent random input, change the estimator, or omit $dF$.

Let
\[
 \ell_m=\zeta^T\Lambda\zeta,\qquad
 \ell_P=\operatorname{tr}(\Sigma^{-1}X\Sigma^{-1}X)
      -\operatorname{tr}(C^{-1}TXT^TC^{-1}TXT^T),
\]
\[
 \chi=z^T\Lambda z=V+s^TQ^{-1}s-V^+.
\]
All three are nonnegative. Moreover,
\[
 \boxed{\|f\|_{C^{-1}}^2\le\frac{\chi}{2}\ell_P.}          \tag{PS6}
\]
To prove this without independent norms, whiten the channel to
$U=C^{-1/2}T\Sigma^{1/2}$. Since $UU^T=I$, $\Pi=I-U^TU$ is an orthogonal
projector. With $Z=\Sigma^{-1/2}X\Sigma^{-1/2}$ and
$h=\Pi\Sigma^{-1/2}z$, one has $|h|^2=\chi$ and
\[
 \ell_P=2\|UZ\Pi\|_F^2+\|\Pi Z\Pi\|_F^2,\qquad
 \|f\|_{C^{-1}}^2=|UZh|^2.
\]
These two formulas prove (PS6), keeping $D,F_1,Q_1$ together inside the
same lost covariance directions.

\paragraph{Signed causal work, not a new independent disturbance.}
Expansion of the augmented input storage gives $W+\mathcal A_{aux}$, where
\[
\begin{split}
 \mathcal A_{aux}={}&-2\eta^TF_1^TQ^{-1}s
 +s^TQ^{-1}F_1PF_1^TQ^{-1}s+\nu^TQ^{-1}\nu\\
 &+2\lambda\operatorname{tr}(Q^{-1}F_1PF_1^T)
 +\lambda\operatorname{tr}(Q^{-1}Q_1Q^{-1}Q_1).
\end{split}                                                   \tag{PS7}
\]
Consequently the literal process joint storage obeys
\[
 \boxed{W^+-W=\mathcal A_{aux}-\ell_m-\lambda\ell_P
       +2\langle T\zeta,f\rangle_{C^{-1}}+\|f\|_{C^{-1}}^2.} \tag{PS8}
\]
In particular,
\[
 W^+-W\le\mathcal A_{aux}-\ell_m
       -(\lambda-\chi/2)\ell_P
       +2\langle T\zeta,f\rangle_{C^{-1}}.                  \tag{PS9}
\]
The signed cross term is still present in (PS9); it has \emph{not} been
absorbed for free. Any further Young inequality consumes additional loss.
Likewise the positive terms in (PS7) must not be maximized separately from
$\ell_P$ or the cross term: they can contain cancelling coordinate work.
Equations (PS7)--(PS8) are the consistent grouping for that comparison.
This is an alternative exact accounting of the same process substep, not
an additional decrement to add to its earlier base loss.

\paragraph{Consistent state-dependent AW coordinates.}
For the retained endpoint frames $\mathsf L,\mathsf L^+$, use
$\widetilde F=\mathsf L^+F\mathsf L^{-1}$,
$\widetilde Q=\mathsf L^+Q(\mathsf L^+)^T$ and
$\widetilde s=\mathsf L^+s$. Then (PS1)--(PS3) are coordinate invariant:
$\widetilde a=\mathsf L^{-T}a$, the action transforms by congruence,
and $\chi,s^TQ^\dagger s$ are unchanged (the supported-action interpretation
is essential for singular Q). With $\Omega=\mathsf L^{-1}d\mathsf L$, retain
\[
\begin{split}
 d\widetilde F&=\mathsf L^+(dF+\Omega^+F-F\Omega)\mathsf L^{-1},\\
 d\widetilde Q&=\mathsf L^+(dQ+\Omega^+Q+Q(\Omega^+)^T)(\mathsf L^+)^T,\\
 d\widetilde s&=\mathsf L^+(ds+\Omega^+s).
\end{split}                                                   \tag{PS11}
\]
Substitute these \emph{together} with the full transformed input derivatives
in (PS8). All endpoint connection work is then already in the storage and
signed auxiliary terms. Add only the retained quotient gauge adjustment;
there is no second independent frame penalty. On a regular operation its
terminal frame is causally available from that operation, not a replayed
future coefficient.

\paragraph{Causal auxiliary and source lift.}
Let $\kappa_i$ contain the actual private frontend/tuner, reference, gate,
clock and pending-target variables. On a fixed regular event stratum their
literal update $\kappa_{i+1}=g_i(x_i,P_i,\kappa_i,u_i)$ gives
\[
 d\kappa_{i+1}=D_xg_i\,dx_i+D_Pg_i\,D_i
                    +D_\kappa g_i\,d\kappa_i+D_ug_i\,du_i. \tag{PS10}
\]
Initial auxiliary/source variations and FAST primitive endpoints are carried,
not reset. The proved one-way default Complementary tuner permits deleting
$D_xg_i,D_Pg_i$ only for that private tuner/clock/target subpath; it does not
delete reference/gate feedback. In (PS4), use derivatives of the literal
coefficient maps composed with (PS10). In particular, shipping
\texttt{time\_update} uses $\omega=gyr-\widehat b_g$ in its actual AG
transition/noise branches, the same committed $(\tau,\Sigma_{aw},h)$ in
both integrated LIN maps, and the actual active/held BA transition and noise.
BG projection precedes these maps; pending AW covariance addition and the
progress-preserving $S$ event follow them. They stay separate in this word.
No ideal Rodrigues or ideal OU coefficients replace the literal polynomial
branches. The derivative $s_1$ retains physical comparison/model and chart
terms and the same source variation. At a branch crossing use a qualified
finite increment, not (PS10) without a proved branch margin.

Substitution of this one causal lift into (PS8), together with the retained
correction/reset/AW/quotient identities, bounds the \emph{same} generated
remainder in (CP7). All covariance ports created now still enter later
$U_iq_{i+1,N}$ terms. The required uniform estimates are now on the combined
budget (PS3) and signed grouped work (PS8), not independently on $dK,r,P$,
loss/source scores, or auxiliary coordinates. Their source-uniform upper
bounds and comparison with the strictly transverse part of (CP5) remain
\textbf{OPEN}. No positive $c_{complete}$ or invariant radius is asserted.

Structures preserved: literal prediction and physical mismatch, all 21
coordinates, actual noise/transition branches, causal auxiliary/source
variations, held support and full generated covariance suffixes. Relaxations:
regular real-operation derivatives; supported-noise restriction explicitly
checked, with unsupported directions retained separately. The augmented
factorization is exact algebra, not a surrogate history. No new shipping
counterexample or numerical exploration is introduced.

\subsection{Uniform held-bias score and the minimal remaining budget domain}
\label{app:held-score-boundary}

\paragraph{Quantifiers and role.}
Consider every finite regular word wholly inside the reached default CoG
held-BA branch, with no release, external covariance write, or initialization
jump inside the word. The nominal held bias is constant and feasible for its
projection, and $P_b\succ0$ is its actual frozen covariance. Physical bias is
the same SLOW history throughout, with amplitude $B_s$ and rate $D_s$ from
the retained contract; FAST remains delivered measurement forcing. This
lemma bounds an unsupported score without charging it against active process
loss. It is not an A21 gap, nor a theorem that held bias becomes observable.
No compactness of nominal AW, reference or attitude error is needed for this
held-coordinate statement. Those open domains are not silently assumed for
the active budget below.

\paragraph{Literal block structure and signed boundary cancellation.}
The reached hold proof above gives, in active/held coordinates,
\[
 P_i=\operatorname{diag}(P_{X,i},P_b),\quad
 B_i=\operatorname{diag}(B_{X,i},I),\quad X\in\mathbb R^{18}.       \tag{HB1}
\]
The additive accelerometer base uses $H_X$ and $R_{\rm eff}=R_a+P_b$,
not an unmasked 21-state gain. Its gain score has zero held component.
Prediction has identity BA transition and zero BA noise; reset, AW, magnetic
and $S$ operations preserve (HB1). Physical held BA increments can therefore
be separated algebraically from prediction as mean shifts in that block.
They commute with its active operation; no new estimator operation is added.
For $e_{b,i}=\widehat b-b_s(t_i)$ the complete held score is consequently
\[
 q_{u,b}=\sum_iP_b^{-1}(e_{b,i}-e_{b,i+1})
       =P_b^{-1}\{b_s(t_N)-b_s(t_0)\},\qquad q_{u,X}=0.          \tag{HB2}
\]
This is exact telescoping, not a sum of absolute increments. For any proved
actual comparison $P_b^{-1}\preceq j_b I$ and word duration $T$,
\[
 \boxed{q_{u,b}^TP_bq_{u,b}\le
 j_b\min\{D_s^2T^2,4B_s^2\}.}                                \tag{HB3}
\]
Indeed the increment is the integral of the same rate-bounded SLOW history
and the difference of two amplitude-bounded endpoints. A return of that
history to its initial value gives zero score, however many intermediate
increments occurred. The bound is independent of event count and of the
time already spent in H18. For the unchanged real core initialization
$\sigma_{bacc,0}=.004$, when that covariance is inherited unchanged,
$j_b=62500$; at $T=60$ and $D_s=.001$ the rate part is exactly $225$.
This is a qualified core-profile value, not a replacement for a caller's
actual $P_b$, a binary32 rounding certificate, or an affordability claim.

On a differentiable family staying in (HB1), $dP_i$ is block diagonal and
$U_i=\operatorname{diag}(U_{X,i},0)$. Thus neither $M dP_0q_{u}$ nor any
generated $M_{N,i+1}U_iq_{u,i+1}$ has an active component. The AW shear acts
only inside $X$, so the conclusion is unchanged in consistent AW coordinates.
It does \emph{not} remove the physical held bias from $r$, $dr$, or
$\delta_X=r+H_Xe_X$, and does not remove $dP_b$ from $dR_{\rm eff}$.
Those are genuine active correction ports and remain in the full suffix word.
There is no assertion that a moving physical quotient projector preserves
this active/held split.

\paragraph{The held work is a boundary term, not active dissipation.}
Let $\Delta b=b_s(t_N)-b_s(t_0)$ and, along such a differentiable family,
$h=d\Delta b-dP_bP_b^{-1}\Delta b$. The held Fisher storage is unchanged,
and direct substitution in the information shear gives
\[
 \eta_{b,N}=\eta_{b,0}-h,\qquad
 W_{b,N}-W_{b,0}=-2\eta_{b,0}^TP_b^{-1}h+h^TP_b^{-1}h.          \tag{HB4}
\]
All intermediate signed cross/square work cancels to this one boundary
expression. The time-rate bound on $b_s$ bounds $\Delta b$, not the derivative
$d\Delta b$ with respect to an arbitrary history-family parameter. Such
source tangents need their specified source coordinates/charge; neither a
pseudoinverse nor the active Schur loss may erase them. This distinction is
necessary even though the finite physical score bound (HB3) is uniform.

\paragraph{A precise necessary activation quantity for the active budget.}
For every supported process substep of (PS1), write $J_+=(FPF^T+Q)^{-1}$,
$L=J-F^TJ_+F$, and define
\[
 E_i=e^TLe,\quad S_i=s^TQ^\dagger s-s^TJ_+s,\quad
 C_i=e^TF^TJ_+s.                                               \tag{HB5}
\]
The range hypothesis is checked before using $Q^\dagger$. Applying (PS1)
also at $e=0$ proves $S_i\ge0$ and that $F^TJ_+s$ is in the range of $L$,
with squared dual loss norm $S_i$. Consequently, on the actual covered word,
\[
 \begin{gathered}
 E_L=\sum E_i,\quad S_q=\sum S_i,\quad C_W=\sum C_i,\\
 \boxed{B_W=E_L+S_q-2C_W},\qquad C_W^2\le E_LS_q,\\
 (\sqrt{E_L}-\sqrt{S_q})^2\le B_W
                  \le(\sqrt{E_L}+\sqrt{S_q})^2.                \tag{HB6}
 \end{gathered}
\]
Proof: expand the squared loss norm of $Le-F^TJ_+s$ and apply Cauchy--Schwarz
only to the stacked same-operation loss vectors. The middle equality retains
every signed comparison/source cross term. The outer bounds are used here to
identify the missing domain, not to price the final Schur gap. If $S_q$ has a
uniform finite cap, a uniform finite $B_W$ exists if and only if the
\emph{process-loss projection energy} $E_L$ has a uniform finite cap.
For example $E_L\le2B_W+2S_q$ and $B_W\le2E_L+2S_q$ prove both implications.
This does not require a box for every coordinate or a bound on loss-kernel
components, but neither does positive process loss supply its own bound on
the comparison occupying those directions.

On the held stratum use (HB5)--(HB6) on $X$ with the actual active process.
The exact signed telescope is
\[
 \begin{split}
 B_{X,W}={}&V_{X,0}-V_{X,N}+\sum_{\rm covered}s_X^TQ_X^\dagger s_X\\
 &+\sum_{\rm correction}(\delta_X^TR_{\rm eff}^{-1}\delta_X-\mathrm{NIS})
   +\sum_{\rm uncovered}(V_{X,i+1}-V_{X,i}).
 \end{split}                                                   \tag{HB7}
\]
For non-accelerometer corrections $R_{\rm eff}$ denotes their actual noise.
No $V_{b,0}$ penalty or sum of held-bias variation energies is needed in
(HB7). The physical $S$ defect remains $-S_{\rm physical}$. BG projection,
reset/chart mismatch and release are not covered by (HB2); their scores and
signed work remain explicit.

\paragraph{What the attempted uniform closure does not establish.}
The source-only supported LIN action has its existing finite sampling-fidelity
bound, but the general activated word lacks a proved cap on $E_L$ and on the
remaining AG/chart/source support terms. The first-Live energy implication
does not supply these recurring bounds. Held LIN BIBO does not, by itself,
bound the full AG/reference/precision comparisons or their causal tangents.
In particular (HB6) cannot be promoted to a numerical uniform $B_W$ by
substituting the source-only action for $E_L$.

The grouped process work (PS8), including its feedback cross term, must still
be composed with correction, BG/reset, reference/noise, AW and gauge work
against the exact complementary Schur loss (CP5). (HB4) removes repeated
pricing of held-coordinate work, not this remaining active domination.
No positive uniform directional score margin or complete gap is established.
The unclosed sufficient proof is class D, not a shipping counterexample.
No radius is calculated. Structures preserved: all 21 states, reached masks,
actual effective noise, complete generated suffixes, inherited SLOW/FAST and
physical $S$, and both AW frames. Relaxations: regular real-operation scope
and an explicitly qualified held-covariance ceiling; no new physical premise.

\subsection{Planar even prediction work without independent parameter charges}
\label{app:planar-even-process-work}

\paragraph{Scope and finite-error role.}
For every regular real-operation prediction on the exact planar stratum,
consider MEKF-root variations preserving that stratum, with the same delivered
record and inherited private frontend, tuner and clocks. Project BG first as
shipping does, and differentiate the prediction from that boundary. Keep
projection, pending AW synchronization, $S$ events, release and reference/gate
changes as separate literal operations. This result reduces the actual process
work in (PS8); it does not bound the inherited $E_L$ or the complete Schur gap.
It is not a claim about general 21-state perturbations or varying source/private
histories. The odd covariance block and its BG-dependent ports remain present.

\paragraph{Exact coefficient cancellation.}
Let $w=\omega_y e_y$ and $W=[w]_\times$. The literal Rodrigues/integral
formulas are polynomials in $I,W,W^2$ with their implemented coefficient
functions. Since $We_y=W^2e_y=0$, both coefficient branches give exactly
\[
 R(h)e_y=e_y,\quad B(h)e_y=h e_y,\quad
 \left(\int_0^h B(s)\,ds\right)e_y=\tfrac12h^2e_y.             \tag{EP1}
\]
With the stated isotropic gyro/bias process densities $q_g,q_b>0$, the
implemented Simpson rule integrates the squared pitch entry $s^2$ exactly.
The pitch/BG block is therefore
\[
 F_y=\begin{bmatrix}1&h\\0&1\end{bmatrix},\qquad
 Q_y=\begin{bmatrix}q_gh+q_bh^3/3&q_bh^2/2\\q_bh^2/2&q_bh\end{bmatrix}.
                                                                    \tag{EP2}
\]
Its determinant is $q_gq_bh^2+q_b^2h^4/12>0$. A regular real spectral repair
of another parity block leaves this positive invariant block unchanged;
solver failure and arithmetic repair defects are not covered by that statement.
The fast $Q_{base}h$ option is also independent of $\omega_y$, but (EP2) uses
the deployed structured option. Literal LIN and BA process coefficients use
the same committed parameters and fixed activation branch. The proved one-way
private-tuner dependence consequently gives, on the 12-dimensional even block,
\[
 dF_E=0,\qquad dQ_E=0.                                       \tag{EP3}
\]
Held BA uses the active block and retained held ports. There is no independent
$d\tau$, $d\sigma$, or $d\Sigma_{aw}$ charge for this fixed-input variation.
There is also no assertion $dF_O=dQ_O=0$: the odd block contains $W$ itself.

\paragraph{The literal quaternion prevents setting $ds_E=0$.}
On $|x|<1/100$, with signed $x=h\omega_y$, the source normalizes the quaternion
with scalar and signed vector components
\[
 w_q=1-x^2/8+x^4/384,\qquad v_q=x/2-x^3/48+x^5/3840.
\]
Its real-operation lifted angle is $\alpha(x)=2\arctan(v_q/w_q)$,
not exactly $x$. Exact differentiation and polynomial multiplication give
\[
 \begin{gathered}
 D_q=w_q^2+v_q^2=1+x^6/23040-x^8/245760+x^{10}/14745600,\\
 1-\alpha'(x)=
 \frac{x^6(1920-80x^2+x^4)}{14745600D_q},\qquad
 0\le1-\alpha'(x)\le\frac{x^6}{7680}.                         \tag{EP4}
 \end{gathered}
\]
Indeed $D_q\ge1$, and the numerator's parenthesis lies in $(0,1920]$ on
this branch. The normalization cancels from the angle ratio; it is not ignored.
The exact planar delivered gyro has $|\omega_{meas,y}|\le\pi/500<.007$;
post-projection $|\widehat b_{g,y}|\le.5$ and $h\le.006$ imply this branch.
This is real-operation algebra; rounded coefficients, FMA and normalization
error still require the separate shipping float32 transfer.

Use the local comparison chart whose homogeneous pitch/BG covariance
transport is (EP2). With physical history fixed, all even model-defect
derivatives vanish except the mean/covariance pitch discrepancy
\[
 ds_E=h\{\alpha'(x)-1\}\,E_{\theta_y}\,d\widehat b_{g,y}.     \tag{EP5}
\]
Here $d\widehat b_{g,y}$ is taken \emph{after} the literal BG projection;
its derivative is not assumed to be one across a projection face. Chart wraps
and event-branch changes require their separate finite-increment treatment.

\paragraph{Uniform auxiliary charge and the signed terms still unpaid.}
Substitute (EP3)--(EP5) into (PS7), in these original process coordinates.
The entire even auxiliary charge reduces to
\[
 \begin{split}
 \mathcal A_{aux,E}
 &=\frac{h\{1-\alpha'(x)\}^2}{q_g+q_bh^2/12}
                  (d\widehat b_{g,y})^2\\
 &\le\frac{h x^{12}}{7680^2q_g}(d\widehat b_{g,y})^2
 <10^{-27}(d\widehat b_{g,y})^2.
 \end{split}
 \tag{EP6}
\]
The last strict rational inequality uses $h\le3/500$, $|x|<1/100$ and
$q_g\ge10^{-6}$, satisfied by the stated $.00135$ gyro-density profile.
No extremum of $P$, $K$, residual, or tuner component was multiplied into it.
The exact denominator retains the same pitch/BG process covariance.

This does \emph{not} pay the process score feedback. With $a_E$ the actual
combined score from (PS1), $u_E=ds_E$, and $D_E=dP_E$, the direct grouped
identity is
\[
 \begin{split}
 W_E^+-W_E={}&-\ell_{mean,E}(\eta_E)-\lambda\ell_{P,E}(D_E)\\
 &+2\langle F_E\eta_E,F_ED_Ea_E+u_E\rangle_{J_E^+}
             +\|F_ED_Ea_E+u_E\|_{J_E^+}^2.
 \end{split}
 \tag{EP7}
\]
In particular the cross term between $F_ED_Ea_E$ and $u_E$ remains signed.
For varying physical/private histories, use the full causal $dF,dQ,ds$ from
(PS10), not (EP3). In AW coordinates these zero original coefficient ports
become the exact frame-connection differences (PS11); they cancel only upon
the full consistent word composition, with both endpoints retained.

The desired uniform bound on $E_L$, the odd and varying-source work, and the
domination of (EP7) plus correction/reset/reference/AW/gauge work by (CP5)
are still \textbf{OPEN}. The number in (EP6) is not a contraction constant.
In particular $d\widehat b_{g,y}=\eta_{g,y}+(dPJe)_{g,y}$; converting its
square to joint storage still uses the inherited comparison and actual metric.
No independent-maxima estimate or invariant radius is substituted for that
missing comparison. Structures preserved: all states/parities, literal process
polynomials and normalized quaternion, causal tuner, physical model mismatch,
and separate projection/reset/AW chronology. Relaxations: explicitly fixed
input, planar, regular real-operation derivative scope only; no physical
assumption or runtime change. The tempting $ds_E=0$ shortcut is invalidated
by the source algebra, not adopted as a surrogate.

\subsection{Bordered comparison storage and its coercivity obstruction}
\label{app:bordered-comparison-storage}

\paragraph{Scope, obligation and qualifications.}
For every finite regular real-operation history with actual SPD covariance,
write $V=e^TP^{-1}e$ and introduce a \emph{proof scalar} $\kappa$, not an
estimator state. Start once with $\kappa_0=V_0+c_0$, $c_0>0$. No upper bound
on $V_0$ is assumed. The following analytical identities absorb the complete
covariance-induced score work on fixed-operand prediction and optimal additive
correction substeps. They do not assume that the actual coefficient/source
derivatives vanish. Reached held BA uses the proved active reduction and its
effective noise; unsupported held/source directions remain separate. The
purpose is to test a new storage rather than repeat the unclosed scalar
budget estimate. All-time coercivity and full endogenous-work absorption are
tested below, not inferred from a nonincreasing expression.

\paragraph{Exact storage --- PROVED analytical.}
Define
\[
 \mathcal P=\begin{pmatrix}P&e\\e^T&\kappa\end{pmatrix},\quad
 c=\kappa-V>0,\quad \mathcal D=d\mathcal P,
 \quad \mathcal W=\operatorname{tr}(\mathcal P^{-1}\mathcal D
                                      \mathcal P^{-1}\mathcal D).
\]
Block elimination, with $J=P^{-1}$, gives
\[
 \mathcal P=\begin{pmatrix}I&0\\e^TJ&1\end{pmatrix}
       \operatorname{diag}(P,c)
       \begin{pmatrix}I&Je\\0&1\end{pmatrix}.
\]
Differentiate this factorization and retain the regression derivative
$d(Je)=J\eta$, where $\eta=de-dPJe$. Its diagonal and off-diagonal
Fisher blocks are orthogonal, so
\[
 \boxed{\mathcal W=\operatorname{tr}(JdPJdP)
       +\frac{2}{c}\eta^TJ\eta+\left(\frac{dc}{c}\right)^2,\qquad
 dc=d\kappa-2e^TJde+e^TJdPJe.}                         \tag{BC1}
\]
This retains every covariance cross entry and the proof-scalar tangent.
Deleting $dc$ or holding this state-dependent decomposition fixed is invalid.

\paragraph{Prediction absorbs its score without a separate residual cap.}
For $P^+=FPF^T+Q$, $e^+=Fe+s$, require $Qt=s$ to be solvable and set
$\kappa^+=\kappa+s^Tt$. Then exactly
\[
 \mathcal P^+=\mathcal A\mathcal P\mathcal A^T+\mathcal U,
 \quad\mathcal A=\operatorname{diag}(F,1),\qquad
 \mathcal U=\begin{pmatrix}Q&s\\s^T&s^Tt\end{pmatrix}\succeq0.
                                                               \tag{BC2}
\]
Indeed $\mathcal U=\binom{I}{t^T}Q(I,t)$. From (PS1),
\[
 c^+=c+\chi,\qquad \chi=V+s^Tt-V^+\ge0.                  \tag{BC3}
\]
For fixed $F,Q,s$ along the considered variation,
$\mathcal D^+=\mathcal A\mathcal D\mathcal A^T$ and
$\mathcal W^+\le\mathcal W$. To prove it, whiten $\mathcal A$ to
$U=(\mathcal P^+)^{-1/2}\mathcal A\mathcal P^{1/2}$.
(BC2) gives $U^TU\preceq I$; for symmetric $Z$,
$\|UZU^T\|_F\le\|Z\|_F$. Thus the entire process score, including
its mixed and square terms, is absorbed in this qualified storage identity.
There is no independent $dP$ times score estimate.

For the actual causal derivatives, put
$\mathcal D_b^+=\mathcal A\mathcal D\mathcal A^T$ and
$\mathcal E=d\mathcal A\mathcal P\mathcal A^T+
\mathcal A\mathcal P d\mathcal A^T+d\mathcal U$.
The exact replacement is
\[
 \mathcal W^+-\mathcal W=-\ell_b+
 2\operatorname{tr}(\mathcal J^+\mathcal D_b^+\mathcal J^+\mathcal E)
 +\operatorname{tr}(\mathcal J^+\mathcal E\mathcal J^+\mathcal E),
 \quad \ell_b\ge0.                                        \tag{BC4}
\]
Here $d\mathcal U$ retains $dQ,ds,d(s^Tt)$ through their actual supported
recurrence; no derivative across a changing support is asserted. These signed
terms are not independent noise or already absorbed work.

\paragraph{Correction is an exact conditional-covariance loss.}
For an actual optimal additive correction define
$S=HPH^T+R$, $K=PH^TS^{-1}$, $r=\delta-He$ and
$\delta=r+He$. Set
\[
 \kappa^+=\kappa+\delta^TR^{-1}\delta-r^TS^{-1}r.           \tag{BC5}
\]
Form $\Sigma=\operatorname{diag}(\mathcal P,R)$ and the invertible map
\[
 L=\begin{pmatrix}I&0&0\\0&1&-\delta^TR^{-1}\\H&0&I\end{pmatrix},
 \qquad Y=L\Sigma L^T.
\]
Partition the last measurement coordinates from the first $n+1$ coordinates.
The measurement block is $S$, the cross block is
$Y_{ay}=\binom{PH^T}{e^TH^T-\delta^T}$, and the Schur complement is
exactly $\mathcal P^+$ with the literal posterior $P^+=P-KHP$ and
$e^+=e+Kr$. The comparison identity gives $c^+=c>0$.
With $B=Y_{ay}S^{-1}$, a second block elimination proves
\[
 \mathcal W(Y)=\mathcal W(\mathcal P^+)
 +\operatorname{tr}(S^{-1}dS S^{-1}dS)
 +2\operatorname{tr}((\mathcal P^+)^{-1}dB S dB^T).         \tag{BC6}
\]
For fixed $H,R,\delta$, congruence invariance gives
$\mathcal W(Y)=\mathcal W(\mathcal P)$, so both displayed losses are
nonnegative. This accounts for the actual gain/residual work with no separate
NIS bound and composes with (BC2) on the same covered word.
The previous $9/10$ magnetic decrement uses a different storage and is not
added here; (BC6) is the correction loss for this candidate.

For actual varying operands set $\Omega=L^{-1}dL$ and
$Z=\Omega\Sigma+\Sigma\Omega^T$. The exact additional input work is
\[
 \operatorname{tr}(R^{-1}dR R^{-1}dR)
 +2\operatorname{tr}(\Sigma^{-1}d\Sigma\Sigma^{-1}Z)
 +\operatorname{tr}(\Sigma^{-1}Z\Sigma^{-1}Z).              \tag{BC7}
\]
This follows by pulling $dY$ back to $d\Sigma+Z$ before squaring.
It retains $dH,dR,d\delta$ with their signs. In particular $d\delta$
contains endogenous curvature and source/reference changes; it is not set
to zero merely because the delivered record is fixed. At the literal $S=0$
update $\delta=-S_{physical}$, and held accelerometer $R$ is its reached
$R_{eff}$ with $dR_{eff}$ retained. No arbitrary masked update is made optimal.

\paragraph{Chronology and the limitation of the candidate.}
Default AW addition is (BC2) with $F=I$, $s=0$, $Q$ its actual PSD increment;
its face/target derivative stays in (BC4). At unsupported projection or
chart/reset steps keep the actual $P^+,e^+$ and choose the bookkeeping update
$\kappa^+=\kappa+V^+-V$, preserving $c$; their full derivatives remain signed
work. This changes no physical or estimator state and supplies no free loss.
Reference, tuner and clocks keep their inherited causal derivatives.

Consequently a covered process/correction word has the exact slack balance
$c_N=c_0+B_W$. This is non-circular positive definiteness at every covered
prefix, \emph{not} uniform comparison retention. It also shows why this
candidate cannot be promoted: the coefficient $2/c_N$ in (BC1) can decrease
without any proved positive lower bound. A bound on each word's $B_W$ alone
does not bound its cumulative sum over infinitely many words.

An exact formal scope test makes this defect explicit. Take the scalar word
\[
 P_0=\tfrac12,\quad e_0=1,\quad F=\tfrac12,\quad
 Q=\tfrac78,\quad s=\tfrac12,\quad H=R=\delta=1.
\]
Prediction gives $P^-=1,e^-=1$, $\chi=2+2/7-1=9/7$.
The correction has $r=0$ and returns $P^+=1/2,e^+=1$, but increases
$\kappa$ by another $1$ and leaves its new slack unchanged. Repeating this
\emph{algebraic} word therefore gives $c_n=c_0+9n/7$ while $V_n=2$.
On $dP=dc=0$, $de=1$, (BC1) equals $4/c_n\to0$ despite fixed mean
comparison tangent energy $2$. This is not a shipping-reachable or admitted
counterexample; it refutes automatic uniform equivalence of the candidate
metric, even for a bounded comparison and a positive observation each word.
This is a comparison on the ambient tangent space. It does not exclude
coercivity on a separately justified restricted causal lift; proving that
comparison, including the scalar tangent, would be an additional obligation.

Nor can the scalar be reset for free. If $c_0$ is fixed along a variation,
restoring $c_N=c_0+B_W$ to $c_0$ with $P_N,e_N$ unchanged changes storage by
\[
 \Delta\mathcal W_{restore}=
 \frac{2B_W}{c_0(c_0+B_W)}\|\eta_N\|_{J_N}^2
 -\frac{(dB_W)^2}{(c_0+B_W)^2}.                            \tag{BC8}
\]
Both terms must stay linked and be paid by actual loss. This proof-only
normalization is not a physical reset or a retention certificate.

\paragraph{Outcome and shipping-faithfulness record.}
The bordered identity genuinely absorbs covered fixed-operand process and
correction score work in one storage. The \textbf{D sufficient-bound failure}
is its unproved uniform coercivity, together with unabsorbed actual ports
(BC4),(BC7), reset/projection/AW and gauge work. It is not an alternative
proof of the regional theorem or a reason to weaken physical assumptions.
No radius is computed. Preserved: complete actual $P,e$, gains, supported
physical/model forcing, Joseph/held qualifications, causal auxiliary history
and every scalar/frame derivative. Relaxations: regular real-operation scope;
fixed operands only for the stated nonexpansion implication, and a clearly
formal scalar scope test. The uniform shipping comparison/word gap remains
\textbf{OPEN}. A useful continuation must pay (BC8) and actual causal work,
or use a uniformly coercive storage; mere monotonicity of $\mathcal W$ does
not suffice.

\subsection{Causal restoration is the original gap, not an extra reserve}
\label{app:bordered-causal-restoration}

\paragraph{Lemma, quantifiers and exact obligation.}
For every finite regular word covered by the preceding bordered lift, propagate
the \emph{complete actual} tangent, including inherited auxiliary/source
coordinates, and start its bookkeeping scalar with $c_0>0$, $dc_0=0$.
Unsupported operations use the explicit slack-preserving bookkeeping and
their full signed work. Let $\mathcal A_B$ be the sum of the nonnegative
bordered base losses from (BC4),(BC6), and let $\mathcal F_B$ be the sum of
all remaining signed work, including (BC7), noise, reset, projection and AW
faces. These are evaluated at actual prefixes, not frozen base products.
Their exact balance is $\mathcal W_N-\mathcal W_0=-\mathcal A_B+
\mathcal F_B$. The proposed refinement asks whether restoring fixed slack
can be paid without the original uniform gap. The following identity answers
that question without estimating any term independently.

\paragraph{Restoration equivalence --- PROVED analytical.}
Put $\lambda=c_0/2$ and retain the original joint storage
$W_\lambda=\eta^TJ\eta+\lambda\operatorname{tr}(JdPJdP)$.
At the root (BC1) gives $\mathcal W_0=2W_{\lambda,0}/c_0$.
At the terminal boundary set $c_N=c_0+B_W$, $dc_N=dB_W$ and let
$\mathcal R_W$ be the signed restoration cost (BC8). Substitution gives
\[
 \boxed{W_{\lambda,0}-W_{\lambda,N}
 =\frac{c_0}{2}\{\mathcal A_B-\mathcal F_B-\mathcal R_W\}.}
                                                               \tag{BR1}
\]
Indeed the terminal $+(dB_W/c_N)^2$ in $\mathcal W_N$ cancels the negative
square in $\mathcal R_W$, and the two mean coefficients sum to $2/c_0$.
No source, covariance or budget derivative is bounded or discarded.
For the justified quotient, append $-\Gamma_0+\Gamma_N$ to (BR1), using
the \emph{original} gauge-energy units. Frame terms are retained in whichever
consistent coordinates are used; no magnetic decrement from a different
storage is added.

Thus proving that bordered loss pays restoration and actual work with a
positive uniform reserve is \emph{exactly} the existing fixed-weight gap.
The negative budget-derivative square cannot also be counted as new available
dissipation. This equivalence is valid for the actual shipping causal lift;
it is not a fixed-coefficient approximation. It neither disproves that gap
nor pays it. Normalizing a proof scalar changes no physical history or state.

\paragraph{Uniform coercivity must be checked on the causal image.}
For one fixed, justified causal root/source lift with coordinate $a$, let
$X_N a=\operatorname{vec}(J_N^{1/2}dP_NJ_N^{1/2})$ (both off-diagonal
entries retained), $Y_Na=J_N^{1/2}\eta_N$, and $b_Na=dc_N$.
All three maps are derivatives of the same inherited execution. For a proposed
$\gamma>0$, uniform domination $\mathcal W_N\ge\gamma W_{\lambda,N}$
requires, and is pointwise equivalent to,
\[
 (1-\gamma\lambda)X_N^TX_N+
 (2/c_N-\gamma)Y_N^TY_N+c_N^{-2}b_N^Tb_N\succeq0           \tag{BR2}
\]
on that lift's allowed coordinate space. Unstored auxiliary inputs are not
silently turned into stored root coordinates. If an allowed $a$ satisfies
$X_Na=0$, $b_Na=0$ and $Y_Na\ne0$, its exact storage ratio is $2/c_N$.
Therefore the scalar budget derivative can recover at most one missing
direction; it cannot automatically control a covariance-invisible mean
subspace of dimension at least two. This is a necessary test, not a claim
that the shipping causal image has that dimension. Proving (BR2) on the
actual compatible stratum still needs a quantitative causal comparison.
Existing magnetic physical-probe service is not such a covariance-tangent
comparison.

\paragraph{A propagated-root scope test, not a freely chosen endpoint.}
The previous ambient test can be strengthened to an exact causal one.
Take two copies of its scalar covariance model:
\[
 P_0=I_2/2,\quad F=I_2/2,\quad Q=7I_2/8,\quad
 H=R=I_2,\quad s=e_1/2,\quad\delta=e_1.
\]
All coefficients and source operands stay fixed. Vary only the comparison
root $e_0(\varepsilon)=e_1+\varepsilon e_2$, with $P_0$ unchanged and
$\kappa_0(\varepsilon)=e_0(\varepsilon)^TP_0^{-1}e_0(\varepsilon)+c_0$.
The actual prediction and gain $K=I_2/2$ give the exact word map
\[
 e_{n+1}=\tfrac14e_n+\tfrac34e_1,\qquad P_{n+1}=P_n=I_2/2.
                                                               \tag{BR3}
\]
At $\varepsilon=0$, $e_n=e_1$, $r_n=0$ and $c_n=c_0+9n/7$.
Differentiation of this \emph{same} causal recurrence gives
$dP_n=0$, $de_n=4^{-n}e_2$. The process scalar increment is source-fixed;
the innovation-square derivative vanishes at $r_n=0$. Since
$d\kappa_0=dV_0=0$, induction gives $d\kappa_n=dc_n=0$. Hence
\[
 \eta_n^TJ_n\eta_n=2\,16^{-n}>0,\qquad
 \frac{\mathcal W_n}{W_{\lambda,n}}
       =\frac{2}{c_0+9n/7}\longrightarrow0.                \tag{BR4}
\]
No terminal direction was independently selected or rescaled. The example
has strictly positive process and observation action and a decaying mean
tangent, yet no uniform metric equivalence on its causal lift. It is a formal
linear covariance example, \emph{not} an OU-III admitted counterexample.
It disproves the inference ``causal propagation alone restores coercivity'';
the actual shipping (BR2) is still OPEN.

\paragraph{Outcome and stopping rule for this refinement.}
Neither (BR1) nor (BR2) supplies the requested uniform bound. This is the one
mathematically motivated refinement of the bordered candidate: its restoration
returns exactly to the original gap, and causality alone does not repair its
metric degeneration. Classification \textbf{D}: an insufficient proof route,
not filter instability. Do not continue growing/resetting the scalar or
tightening isolated coefficients as a substitute for the original linked
comparison. A new argument must bound the actual net word work or establish
a quantitative comparison on the actual causal image. Preserved structures:
all states, actual $P/K$/Joseph and supported process, full derivative and
source/reference/reset/AW/gauge chronology. Relaxations: regular real-operation
scope and the explicitly formal scope test only. No physical premise, runtime
behavior, proof status count, invariant radius or all-time admission changes.

\subsection{The actual locked-Live reference port and its linked source work}
\label{app:locked-live-causal-reference}

\paragraph{Quantifiers and finite-error role.}
Consider any finite continuation on the deployed default Complementary path
with wrapper and inner stages Live, magnetic lock already set, inherited
auxiliary state, and no Cold/reacquisition or external reconfiguration.
The word may contain the scheduled refinement and subsequent continuous
hard-iron updates. Use the actual regular branch derivatives when forming
storage; branch retention itself is not asserted. The following result pays
the \emph{reference-feedback part} of the homogeneous linked work exactly.
It does not assert contraction of the remaining MEKF block. Unlike the failed
bordered-storage shortcut, it uses literal causal dependencies, not a new
bookkeeping reservoir or a uniform equivalence assumption.

\paragraph{Zero reverse reference port --- PROVED analytical.}
Hold fixed the delivered sensor/time history and inherited private frontend,
magnetic acquisition, reference, hard-iron and tuning state. Then throughout
such a continuation, the derivative from the MEKF root mean/covariance to the
reference $B_r$, applied offset $b$, and corrected magnetic input is zero:
\[
 D_{(\widehat x_0,P_0)}(B_{r,i},b_i,m_i-b_i)=0.             \tag{LR1}
\]
This statement concerns parameter/input derivatives. It does \emph{not} set
the attitude-dependent magnetic row or innovation derivative to zero.

Here is the source proof, including the apparent reverse gate. In
\texttt{ProxyStartupFusion::updateTime}, the gravity gate does read
\texttt{attitudeReferenceQuat\_()}, which returns the MEKF attitude in Live.
Its \texttt{gravity\_trusted} result, however, guards only the
\texttt{!mag\_ref\_set\_} acquisition block in \texttt{updateMag}.
That block is inactive on this continuation. Refinement uses
\texttt{impl\_.startupProxyTiltQuat()}, the cached delivered acc/gyro,
corrected magnetic samples, its own statistics and clocks. The private tilt
is the measurement-only Mahony state. Refinement's eligibility, reference
write and completion/hold-release flags have no MEKF reader. Its subsequent
\texttt{writeMekfYaw\_} \emph{does} read current MEKF tilt: that is an actual
estimator jump, retained in the MEKF map, not an input to the learned reference.

Continuous accumulation uses the same private tilt and \emph{raw} magnetic
sample. Its solve, validity flags and slew use only these statistics, the
inherited applied offset/anchor/reference, and time. The wrapper's mirror
\texttt{mag\_world\_ref\_uT\_} is written by
\texttt{setMagWorldRef\_}, never read back from the MEKF. In Live the tilt
watchdog's reset preserves the Live stage and does not call the Cold frontend
reset. Its timing, state jump and branch margins remain estimator obligations.
The direction output has no return into the default tuner. Induction over
the actual call order proves (LR1), including refinement and release.
In fact the induction gives equality of the entire reference executions for
finite MEKF root changes whenever both continuations stay in this qualified
family. Thus no finite-error remainder is hidden in this zero reverse port.
Equivalently, the active auxiliary state $a$ and estimator state $x$ have
the causal form
\[
 a_{i+1}=f_i(a_i,u_i),\qquad x_{i+1}=g_i(x_i,a_i,u_i),\qquad
 \begin{pmatrix}dx_{i+1}\\ da_{i+1}\end{pmatrix}=
 \begin{pmatrix}A_i&B_i\\0&C_i\end{pmatrix}
 \begin{pmatrix}dx_i\\da_i\end{pmatrix}
 +\begin{pmatrix}D_i\\E_i\end{pmatrix}du_i.              \tag{LR2}
\]
Here $x$ retains all MEKF coordinates and endogenous switching/reset state;
$a$ excludes the passive gravity-gate readout while lock holds. These are
\emph{complete} derivatives of the literal maps, not frozen Riccati factors.
The zero lower-left block is not a claim that inherited $a_0$ is independent
of the stored root on every construction-generated lift. Its actual correlated
variation must be propagated, as specified below.
Thus $da_0=du_i=0$ implies $da_i=0$ and exactly zero homogeneous reference
port work, uniformly over this entire qualified family. Reacquisition in
Live may use the MEKF frame and is explicitly outside this proof.

\paragraph{The source reference is paired, not frozen.}
For the real-operation lift of the continuous tracker, write its normalized
same-history statistics as $A=\sum_j w_jR_j/\sum_jw_j$ and
$w=\sum_jw_jR_jm_j/\sum_jw_j$, with $w_j\ge0$ and $R_j$ normalized private
tilt rotations. Define $c(v)=(\|v_{xy}\|,0,v_z)^T$ and retain the actual
anchor $b_a,B_a$. The literal code evaluates both levels against the
\emph{current same statistics}, giving exactly
\[
 B_r=B_a+c(w-Ab)-c(w-Ab_a).                                \tag{LR3}
\]
Canonicalization is globally nonexpansive:
$\|c(v)-c(v')\|^2=(\|v_{xy}\|-\|v'_{xy}\|)^2+(v_z-v'_z)^2
\le\|v-v'\|^2$. Since $\|A\|\le1$ by its rotation average,
\[
 \boxed{\|B_r-B_a\|\le\|A(b-b_a)\|\le\|b-b_a\|.}       \tag{LR4}
\]
This uniform finite-increment bound remains valid at zero horizontal level;
no derivative of a zero norm is used. It retains correlation of the two
level evaluations and proves no reference alignment or magnetic service.

One required domain fact now follows without comparison retention. If the
existing delivered magnetic envelope is $\|m_i\|\le M$, the tracker's
nonnegative exponential statistics give its field RMS at most $M$. Every
accepted estimate obeys the literal $\|b_{\rm est}\|\le\beta M$ gate.
For the default apply fraction one and real $0\le\alpha\le1$, the slew is
a convex combination; rejected updates leave the applied offset unchanged.
Starting from the actual zero applied offset therefore gives
$\|b_i\|\le\beta M$ at every prefix. With default startup hard iron disabled,
acquisition/refinement use nonnegative weighted means of normalized rotations
of the raw record, so $\|B_a\|\le M$. Continuous application starts only
after refinement, hence $b_a=0$ at the first anchor. No subsequent reanchor
occurs on this continuation. Using the represented default
$\beta=\mathrm{RN}_{32}(.35)<7/20$ in (LR4) proves
\[
 \|B_{r,i}\|\le\frac{27}{20}M,\qquad
 \|m_i-b_i\|\le\frac{27}{20}M.                            \tag{LR5}
\]
This is a real-operation, default-configuration amplitude bound conditional
on actual acquisition, not a bound on its time, horizontal alignment, float
accumulation, NIS affordability, or the complete MEKF domain. It introduces
no new physical magnetic envelope. Nondefault startup offsets retain their
actual anchor terms instead of using (LR5).

For the full source derivative let $\ell=w-Ab$, $\ell_a=w-Ab_a$,
$C=Dc(\ell)$, $C_a=Dc(\ell_a)$ and $\Delta b=b-b_a$. Where both horizontal
norms are nonzero, direct differentiation of (LR3) and regrouping prove
\[
 \boxed{dB_r=dB_a+(C-C_a)(dw-dA\,b_a-A\,db_a)
                 -C(dA\,\Delta b+A\,d\Delta b).}          \tag{LR6}
\]
Here $Dc(v)$ has first row $(v_x,v_y,0)/\|v_{xy}\|$, zero second row and
third row $(0,0,1)$. Shared-statistics work cancels exactly when
$\Delta b=d\Delta b=0$, even when $dA,dw$ are nonzero. Away from that case,
neither it nor $dB_a$ is deleted. Zero horizontal norms require (LR4) or a
valid directional/finite-increment treatment; the final-reference acceptance
gate alone does not bound these two intermediate horizontal denominators.

At the literal magnetic boundary with world-to-body rotation $R$ and fixed
deheel rotation $D_h$, the paired input/reference source port is
\[
 dr\big|_{\rm source}=D_h(dm-db)-R\,dB_r,\qquad
 dH\big|_{\rm source}=-[R\,dB_r]_\times E_\theta^T.        \tag{LR7}
\]
Its gain/innovation and Joseph derivatives still use the same actual $P$.
Propagate these linked ports through the complete suffix formula, including
every generated $U_iq_{i+1,N}$; (LR4)--(LR5) are not permission to maximize
the terms in (LR7) independently.

\paragraph{What this removes from the word gap.}
On a justified transverse root lift, let $\mathsf M$ be the complete
homogeneous MEKF derivative with inherited $a_0,u$ fixed, and let $f$ be
the terminal response to the actual causal auxiliary/source/gauge variation,
so $v_N=\mathsf Mv_0+f$. All internally generated covariance ports remain
in $\mathsf M$ and $f$. With the same joint metrics $\mathcal J_i$, the
exact transverse gap is
\[
 W_{\perp,0}-W_{\perp,N}
 =v_0^T(\mathcal J_0-\mathsf M^T\mathcal J_N\mathsf M)v_0
 -2(\mathsf Mv_0)^T\mathcal J_N f-f^T\mathcal J_N f
 -\Gamma_0+\Gamma_N.                                     \tag{LR8}
\]
Use the actual endpoint gauge energies, with source/reference dependence
retained; $C_Q\alpha$ belongs to $f$ when gauge is separated from the
transverse root. The physical-distance conversion still requires the moving
projector derivative. If the reference is varied, its contribution to $f$
is (LR6)--(LR7), not zero. If it is fixed on the homogeneous lift, the
reference-feedback part is zero by (LR1). Neither statement deletes attitude
row feedback, reset work or physical OU/S/bias forcing.
Inherited endogenous switch/clock directions not included in the stored root
are retained in $f$; (LR8) makes no mean/$P$-only Markov claim across unproved
branch changes. In the planar wrapper $D_h=I$; no transfer to another profile
or varying installation transform is implicit.

Specifically, propagate the lower block of (LR2) causally and let
$\mathsf R_a$ denote the resulting terminal joint-state reader of $da_0$.
If the \emph{actual} inherited lift has $da_0=\Lambda v_0+\zeta$, then
\[
 \mathsf M_{\rm lift}=\mathsf M+\mathsf R_a\Lambda,
 \qquad f_{\rm lift}=\mathsf R_a\zeta+f_{\rm later\ source}. \tag{LR9}
\]
Use these two objects in (LR8). The generated root contribution
$\mathsf R_a\Lambda v_0$ is endogenous and keeps all its signed cross terms;
it cannot be charged as independent source noise or set to zero by (LR1).
If no such single-valued graph is justified, retain the full augmented lift
instead of inventing $\Lambda$. In particular an acquisition first reached
in Live can inherit MEKF-frame dependence even though the subsequent locked
reference recurrence has no reverse edge. No construction state is restarted.

\textbf{Remaining obstruction:} no uniform positive margin for the first
quadratic form in (LR8) on the justified transverse lift, nor affordable
domination of its grouped source/gauge terms, has been established. The new
zero port and amplitude bound discharge specific causal/domain dependencies;
they are not the requested complete net-work domination. No radius is solved.
Structures preserved: all shipping states/covariance/gains, reference/offset
pairing, refinement yaw write, watchdog and branch conditions, source history
and endpoint gauge. Relaxations: qualified regular Live derivative and
explicit real-arithmetic reference bounds; no estimator or premise changes.
The unclosed complete-gap attempt remains class D, not instability.

\subsection{The complete coupled process matrix and an actual AW-face obstruction}
\label{app:odd-covariance-signed-gap}

\paragraph{Six questions before the calculation.}
(1) The controlling inequality is still
\[
 B^T(G_{action}-G_{port}-\Gamma_0+\Gamma_N)B
                 \succeq c_{complete}B^T\mathcal J_{\perp,0}B,
 \qquad c_{complete}>0.                                    \tag{OF0}
\]
Equivalently use the exact signed balance (CP7), with its already-paid
complementary base packets. (2) The attacked terms are the combined process
score, its generated cross/square work, and the original-marginal AW-face
derivative inside that same matrix. (3) The calculation is substituted into
the process entries of (OF0) and its central-planar odd-covariance partial
block, not into a second storage. (4) On the qualified pure odd-covariance
fibre the score and every non-AW generated self-port vanish by the shipping
equations; the remaining AW work is one explicit stacked regression reader.
It is retained with the actual transported process/$S$/magnetic Fisher action.
(5) Its exact relative Schur threshold is one in (OF5) below, with a common
positive reserve required for a uniform margin. (6) This reduces the
generated-port obligation on that partial block to a specified operator.
It does not discharge the machine-readable full-word OPEN dependency:
the even/source cross blocks and the shipping reader bound remain unproved.
An explicit D-class failure of automatic absorption is proved below.

\paragraph{One common coordinate matrix, before any norm.}
Choose a basis of the \emph{existing justified} root/source tangent lift;
write its coordinate as $a$. Include the inherited auxiliary coordinates and
their causal maps from (PS10),(LR2),(LR9), rather than setting their correlated
root derivatives to zero. For the $j$th basis vector retain the complete
prefix $\eta_{i,j},D_{i,j}$ and all literal ports. With $\mathsf L_i$ the
joint dissipative base and $p_{i,j}$ its complete signed port, put
$\mathcal Q_i=\mathcal J_i-\mathsf L_i^T\mathcal J_{i+1}\mathsf L_i$.
The full matrix
has entries exactly
\[
\begin{split}
 (G_{action}-G_{port})_{jk}=\sum_i\{&
 v_{i,j}^T\mathcal Q_i v_{i,k}\\
 &-(\mathsf L_iv_{i,j})^T\mathcal J_{i+1}p_{i,k}
   -p_{i,j}^T\mathcal J_{i+1}\mathsf L_iv_{i,k}
   -p_{i,j}^T\mathcal J_{i+1}p_{i,k}\}.
\end{split}                                                   \tag{OF1}
\]
Here $v=(\eta,D)$, with both off-diagonal covariance entries counted.
Append $-\Gamma_0+\Gamma_N$ without discarding its source derivatives.
The actual prefix is used, including pending/face, scheduler and projection
state. The suffix implementation is (WS5)--(WS6), including $U_iq_{i+1,N}$.
Thus (OF1) retains process mismatch, coefficient derivatives, $dK r$,
source/reference/noise, correction defects, reset/projection, AW and endpoint
gauge work on the same coordinates. No frozen-factor product defines $v_i$.

There is a useful explicit process entry. Use \emph{exactly} (PS5)--(PS8)'s
$\Sigma,T=[F,I],\Lambda,z=(e,s),X_j,\zeta_j$, and put
$f_j=T X_j\Lambda z$. Its entry in the local gap is
\[
\begin{split}
 &\zeta_j^T\Lambda\zeta_k+
 \lambda\operatorname{tr}(\Sigma^{-1}X_j\Sigma^{-1}X_k)\\
 &\quad-\lambda\operatorname{tr}(J^+TX_jT^TJ^+TX_kT^T)\\
 &\quad-(\mathcal A_{aux})_{jk}\\
 &\quad-(T\zeta_j)^TJ^+f_k-f_j^TJ^+T\zeta_k-f_j^TJ^+f_k.
\end{split}
                                                               \tag{OF1a}
\]
$(\mathcal A_{aux})_{jk}$ is the polarization of the actual (PS7) quadratic,
including $dF,dQ,ds$. The same process information matrix satisfies
$z^T\Lambda z=\chi=E_i+S_i-2C_i$. Consequently (OF1a) combines
$E_L,S_q,-2C_W$ with generated cross/square work \emph{before} using the
Fisher square bound. It needs no independent cap on $E_L$ to be formed.
The equivalence between finite caps in (HB6) is a statement about that
\emph{scalar budget}, not a necessary intermediate step for every possible
proof of (OF0). No full-gap sign is inferred from this observation.

For the conditional/complementary partition of the existing root lift,
insert (CP3)--(CP5) in (OF1). This removes base complementary propagation
from the adverse budget with coefficient one. It retains $S_b$ and every
actual generated cross term; neither a half-charge nor another propagation
penalty is added. Use (CM4) when its actual $C,T,q_a$ reader is needed.
Its uniform margin remains OPEN. The analysis now asks what (OF1) actually
does on one invariant causal partial block.

\paragraph{The shipping pure odd-covariance fibre.}
Take a regular central $\beta=0$ planar CoG A21 continuation after refinement,
with no external write, Cold/reacquisition, hold/release or frame-retargeting
jump inside the word. Keep the actual delivered/private/reference/tuner,
$S$/AW clocks, pending target and physical history fixed, with isotropic
default AW target. The odd indices are
$(0,2,3,5,7,10,13,16,19)$; the nominal mean and central comparison have zero
odd component and $P$ is parity block diagonal. Vary only symmetric $P_O$.
Apply this partial derivative on its intersection with the actual justified
causal lift. Its ambient symmetric dimension is 45; this is \emph{not} a
claim that construction admits 45 independent covariance inputs. Inherited
auxiliary/root correlations on other directions still use (LR9).

At acc/mag corrections the odd measurement channel is $y$, while $r_y=0$;
at $S$ the same conclusion is $r_{S,y}=0$. The innovation and gain split by
parity, so $dK_O r_y=0$ and the even gain/residual are unchanged. All nominal
mean, BG/BA projections, attitude injections and reset operands therefore
remain identical. The sensor-only tuner and locked reference remain identical
by their proved causal zero edges. Induction in literal call order gives
$de=0,dF=dQ=dH=dR=dG=ds=0$ on this fibre. The statement about odd process
coefficients is limited to this \emph{pure covariance} variation: even
$d\widehat b_{g,y}$ still generates odd coefficient work in the other blocks.
No held effective-noise derivative is deleted; the present fibre is A21.
Solver repair, gate/face crossings and arithmetic are separately qualified.

Since $e_O=0$, $DJe=0$, $\eta=0$, and $q_O=0$ at every suffix. Thus the
process score and each generated $U_iq_{i+1,N}$ have zero odd self-block
contribution, including the AW increment's score contribution. The nominal
\emph{full} $E_L$ need not be zero or bounded: its score reader on this
fibre is zero. Every non-AW covariance operation has the actual differential
$D^+=F_ODF_O^T$, $D^+=A_OD A_O^T$, or $D^+=G_ODG_O^T$.
These are the \emph{complete partial derivatives}, because the possible
coefficient feedback has just been proved zero, not assumed frozen.
They retain the actual integrated $a_w\to v\to p\to S$ chain and all nine
odd covariance coordinates. Reset is a Fisher isometry on its invertible
branch. Mean projection preserves covariance on this fibre.

Both existing proof frames have $dL=0$ here. Fisher congruence invariance
therefore evaluates the same $W$ in the recovered original odd coordinates;
there is no extra endpoint connection or mean gauge energy on this fibre.
No new metric equivalence, physical quotient or gauge deletion is used.

\paragraph{Exact completion of the actual active face.}
In $P_O$, take $a=AW_y$ and $o=$ its other eight coordinates. Use the
\emph{existing} (CA1) $B,T,C$, and denote the regression energy by
$\beta=TBT^T$ here; this is not the physical roll parameter above.
At a strictly active target-fixed face let $\Delta=\sigma^2-P_{aa}>0$.
Shipping retains $B,P_{ao}$ and sets $P_{aa}^+=\sigma^2$; hence
\[
 C^+=C+\Delta=\sigma^2-\beta,\quad T^+=T,\quad
 dC^+=-d\beta,\quad
 d\beta=T\,dB\,T^T+2dT\,B\,T^T.                          \tag{OF2}
\]
In original coordinates this is precisely $D^+=D-E_aD_{aa}E_a^T$,
the derivative of the \emph{additive PSD increment}, not legacy replacement
of cross covariance. Substitute (OF2) into (CA1), with $\eta=0$:
\[
 \boxed{\frac{W-W^+}{\lambda}
 =\left(\frac{dC}{C}\right)^2
  +2\left(\frac1C-\frac1{C^+}\right)dT B dT^T
  -\left(\frac{d\beta}{C^+}\right)^2.}                       \tag{OF3}
\]
This is an exact conditional/complementary block completion. The conditional
covariance square is positive and has no cross term; all remaining adverse
face work is the one scalar regression derivative. Inactive scalar faces are
the identity. At zero gap use actual finite/directional inclusions, not an
asserted differentiable branch. A varying causal target has
$dC^+=d\sigma^2-d\beta$ and belongs to the full source/cross blocks.

\paragraph{The complete odd matrix, including quantitative directional service.}
On any allowed odd root basis write $D_i=\sum_j y_jD_{i,j}$, where the prefix
maps include \emph{every} preceding AA deletion (OF2). Let $H_0$ be its root
Fisher Gram. At an ordinary operation use the polarized exact Fisher loss
$\operatorname{tr}(J_iD_{i,j}J_iD_{i,k})-
\operatorname{tr}(J_{i+1}D_{i+1,j}J_{i+1}D_{i+1,k})$.
Sum these process and actual acc/$S$/magnetic losses, together with the two
positive face forms in (OF3), into $H_W$. At the actual active faces stack
the rows $(R_W)_{ij}=d\beta_i(D_{i,j})/C_i^+$.
Telescoping proves the exact \emph{complete} partial matrix
\[
 \boxed{G_{OO}=\lambda(H_W-R_W^TR_W),\qquad
 W_0-W_N=\lambda y^T(H_W-R_W^TR_W)y.}                         \tag{OF4}
\]
There is no complementary-base self/mix charge left to pay: these are actual
complete prefixes, and (CP4)'s base propagation is already included in the
telescoped losses. This is a restriction of (OF1), not a different storage.

In particular, for an applied odd scalar magnetic channel the actual row is
$h_m=(-v_z,v_x,0,\ldots,0)$ on $(\theta_x,\theta_z,\ldots)$, with
$v=R B_r$; the actual $S$ row is $h_S=E_{S_y}^T$. For either channel put
$S=hPh^T+R$, using that operation's inherited covariance/noise. Its Fisher
loss, with no radial residual feedback on this fibre, is exactly
\[
 L_{cov}(D)=\frac{2}{S}hD J D h^T-
                       \frac{(hD h^T)^2}{S^2}
 = (Dh^T)^T\left(\frac{2J}{S}-\frac{h^Th}{S^2}\right)(Dh^T).
                                                               \tag{OF4a}
\]
The middle matrix is positive, since $hPh^T<S$. Its actual matrix square
root times $D_{i,j}h_i^T$ gives the \emph{directional} columns in $H_W$.
Thus $S$ and magnetic service enter quantitatively with their actual
innovation whitening and transported directions. On the odd heading/BG
physical probes $\Phi_i$, the service reader is $h_{m,i}\Phi_i/\sqrt{S_i}$;
(OF4a) keeps this same $h_{m,i},S_i$ and chronology, together with the full
covariance prefix. It does not replace that prefix by $\Phi_iX\Phi_i^T$
after a face, nor convert the two-column service floor into a full 45-column
floor. The qualified $9/10$ even magnetic decrement remains in (OF1)'s other
blocks; it is not charged again here. Process loss in $H_W$ retains both AG
and integrated LIN/BA noise. On a regular A21 step with full odd $Q\succ0$
and invertible $F_O$, it is strictly positive on every nonzero covariance
tangent. If this process's complete prefix is injective, it establishes
pointwise $H_W\succ0$ on an injective root basis,
not a uniform margin or an affordable face bound.

For a candidate $c>0$, if $H_W-cH_0\succ0$, two exact Schur complements give
\[
 \boxed{G_{OO}\succeq c\lambda H_0
 \quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
 I-R_W(H_W-cH_0)^{-1}R_W^T\succeq0.}                         \tag{OF5}
\]
The threshold is one for the squared relative singular norm, evaluated on
one word. A common strict reserve plus uniform coercivity of the retained
positive action is needed for a uniform $c$. If the inverse is unjustified,
retain (OF4); do not remove a kernel by pseudoinverse. On the full existing
lift the exact cross block with even/source coordinates remains in (OF1).
After any proved positive $G_{OO}-c\mathcal J_{O,0}$, its Schur reduction
subtracts $G_{EO}(G_{OO}-c\mathcal J_{O,0})^{-1}G_{OE}$ from the remaining
block. Neither the partial zero port nor (OF5) deletes those causal terms.

\paragraph{Analytic offending direction and a failed causal shortcut.}
The remaining reader has a literal generator. In the original odd
$(o,a)$ partition, $F_{ao}=0,F_{aa}=\phi$, while $F_{oa}$ is the nonzero
integrated $v,p,S$ column. Shipping prediction gives
\[
 P_{ao}^-=\phi(P_{ao}F_{oo}^T+P_{aa}F_{oa}^T)+Q_{ao}.        \tag{OF5a}
\]
Its tangent uses the same fixed coefficients on this fibre. At a non-AW
mag/$S$ correction, (CA2) gives
$B^+=(B^{-1}+h_o^TR^{-1}h_o)^{-1}$,
$dB^+=A_o dB A_o^T$, while $T,dT,C,dC$ are unchanged.
Thus $d\beta^+=T dB^+T^T+2dT B^+T^T$ is linked to the exact action
(OF4a). The acc row also observes AW and uses its full ordinary Fisher map.
Equations (OF5a),(CA2),(OF2), in actual service order, generate $R_W$.
No unrelated extrema of the regression, covariance or service directions
may replace them.

At a single face with $T\ne0$, take $dT=dC=0$ and $T dB T^T\ne0$.
(OF3) is strictly negative. Conditional-precision nonincrease cannot imply
Fisher-tangent nonincrease. More importantly, imposing $D_{aa,0}=0$ at an
inherited target does not automatically remove the negative direction after
an anisotropic correction. Here is one exact \emph{formal implication test},
not a shipping-reached or service-admitted history:
\[
 \begin{gathered}
 P_0=\begin{pmatrix}1&0&1\\0&1&1\\1&1&3\end{pmatrix},\quad
 H=(0,1,0),\ R=1,\\
 D_0=\begin{pmatrix}-10&3&-7\\3&1&4\\-7&4&0\end{pmatrix}.
 \end{gathered}
                                                               \tag{OF6}
\]
The AW coordinate is the third. Initially $T=(1,1),C=1$, $dT=0$ and
$dC=-d\beta=3$, with the required $D_{aa,0}=0$. The actual optimal
non-AW correction gives
\[
 P_c=\begin{pmatrix}1&0&1\\0&1/2&1/2\\1&1/2&5/2\end{pmatrix},\quad
 D_c=\begin{pmatrix}-10&3/2&-17/2\\3/2&1/4&7/4\\-17/2&7/4&-15/4\end{pmatrix}.
\]
With no process, floor its AA entry back to 3. On the three $dB$ coordinates,
the exact net matrix is
\[
 \begin{pmatrix}5/9&14/9&8/9\\14/9&41/9&17/9\\8/9&17/9&31/18\end{pmatrix}.
\]
Its first two pivots are $5/9,1/5$, and the remaining Schur pivot is $-3/2$.
The direction $(-10,3,1)$ has net gap $-3/2$, although the correction
has dissipated $39/4$. This is the signed regression term, not independently
maximized positive or auxiliary energies.

Even a strictly positive process does not make that inference valid. Follow
